(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ac-7"] = {"468273101":[["","DL Border Police Interrogation Room"],["","In the darkness, he hears nothing but the sound of his own labored breathing. Blood mixes with sweat as it trickles down his face, stinging his wounds before gathering on his chin and dropping to the floor below in a continuous, steady drip."],["","Tap—tap—tap—"],["","He hears sudden footsteps approaching from afar, stopping outside the room door. The person leisurely opens the door and walks in."],["","Suddenly, he lets out a soft laugh, breaking the husky rhythm of his breathing."],["","The esteemed Mr. Victor Ruark, Commander of the East Milkhama Border Forces Base. It's been a long time."],["","The person who entered paused, clearly not expecting their identity to be discovered so quickly."],["","...How did you know it was me?"],["","Ruark turned on the lights."],["","Behind the interrogation table sat an emaciated man. His hands were cuffed behind the chair, his legs tightly secured with chains."],["","Ruark walked over and sat down across from him, scanning the prisoner from head to toe. Finally, he chuckled, a hint of victorious joy creeping into his eyes."],["","The young man met his gaze with neither humility nor arrogance. He was undoubtedly a prisoner, but he wasn't like the other—his calm demeanor said it all."],["???","The smell of smoke, sir. Last time we sat together to plot our ambitions, you even invited me to try some..."],["???","You said it was a popular silk tobacco from the homeland, sought after by nobles, rare and expensive. I remember it clearly."],["Ruark","Seems I overlooked it... Would you like one now?"],["","Ruark took out a cigarette case from his pocket and gestured to the young man."],["???","A final smoke before the executioner?"],["Ruark","Not really, you're more useful alive than dead. The title of \"Border Defense Commander\" only carried way in the DLAF. To completely control Cross's power and industry, it needs to be in your name."],["","Ruark leisurely lit a cigarette and took a deep drag. The smoke rings he exhaled enveloped the young man tightly."],["","The young man closed his eyes and took a deep breath, the smoke rings were instantly dispersed by the airflow—tobacco helped numb some of the pain, softening his expression."],["???","I see. This was your plan all along. Working together was a pretext for executing this plan, wasn't it?"],["Ruark","Haha, don't be surprised, young man. Everyone screws up eventually. You're no exception."],["","Ruark looked into the young man's eyes and slowly called out a name."],["Ruark","Anything else you want to say? If not, your personal cell is already prepared. Shall I take you to see it?"],["","The young man was silent for a while. Just when Ruark thought he might have passed out, he spoke softly again."],["???","We still have some time, sir... I want to know, throughout it all, did you ever know the whereabouts of the \"treasure\"?"],["Ruark","That doesn't matter. I just needed to make sure you followed my bait straight into the trap..."],["","The young man chuckled after hearing that."],["???","A trap? Haha... Everyone is in the trap, sir. Though not everyone realizes it."],["???","You wanted to catch me, that's the purpose of your elaborate setup—so this conversation we're having, whose purpose is it serving?"],["Ruark","...What do you mean?"],["???","Sir, I want to tell this story from my perspective. I have a feeling now is a good time to talk about those past events, and I promise they will surprise you..."],["???","After all, \"everyone screws up eventually.\""],["","Half a month ago, Samba Tavern"],["","The muddled scent of alcohol, cigarettes, hormones, and perhaps a few days' worth of uncollected trash assaulted Will's nostrils the moment he pulled open the tavern door."],["","He instinctively took a step back, unsure whether to proceed, when a hand suddenly reached out from inside the tavern and yanked him in."],["","With a bang and Will's startled cry, the tavern door closed."],["Mercenary A","Heeey! New guy—hic! You made it just in time! We've been warming up all day. Tonight's the climax of the mobilization meeting—hic! We'll give you a lil' demonstration! Here—have a drink first, yeah?"],["Will","O-okay, I'll have a..."],["","The mercenary casually handed Will a keg. Will seriously underestimated its weight, falling off balance and swaying, much to the delight of the other drinkers."],["","As Will's face turned red and his heart raced, he lost his footing, falling backward. Just then, someone reached out, stopping his fall at the last second."],["???","How'd this kid get in here? Don't you know we booked the place today?"],["Mercenary B","Yo chief, when'd you turn up? Don't worry, this guy's new. Looks like a real stringbean, for sure, but he's got a knack for piloting STs. Even Johnny got played by him!"],["???","Him? Played Johnny? Hahahahahahaha! Johnny, you halfwit!"],["","Will quickly put down the keg, stood up straight, and bowed very respectfully."],["Will","Nice to meet you, Mr. Meritus. I'm Will Sander, a new arrival. I would like to offer my deepest gratitude for the privilege of joining your team, and I promise to devote my utmost effort to the operations that lie ahead."],["Meritus","......"],["","After a brief moment of silence in the tavern, there was a burst of laughter loud enough to lift the roof. Everyone was laughing heartily, and Will's shoulders were patted by countless excited hands. He was bewildered."],["Will","S-sorry! I said something wrong! I-I..."],["Meritus","Alright, alright. Bill, whatever your name is, we don't do that fancy talk here. Just be casual, natural, okay?"],["Meritus","Eat and drink well tonight. Starting tomorrow, follow us and work hard, got it?"],["Will","Got it!"],["","Meritus nodded in satisfaction, bypassed Will, and grabbed four buckets of fried chicken from the bar to leave."],["","Will looked around. He was surrounded by mercenaries, some dead drunk, some still pointing and laughing. Will grabbed some chicken and followed after Meritus."],["Meritus","Why are you following me? Go drink with them."],["","Will didn't say anything, placing the bucket of fried chicken in front of Meritus and refilling his empty glass."],["Meritus","Ah... you want to drink with me? Hahaha! A toothpick like you? Come on. I'd drink you under the table!"],["Will","Not really, boss. I have some questions I'd like to ask you."],["Meritus","What? For tactical issues, go to Johnny. For logistics issues, go to Simon. For personal issues, solve them yourself. Don't interrupt my meal."],["Will","N-no, boss, I just wanted to ask... do you know about the \"treasure\"?"],["","Meritus paused mid-bite and glanced sideways at Will. Will started sweating again, scratching his head one moment and then his nose the next."],["Will","I don't mean anything funny, boss... It's just... h-have you heard the rumors?"],["Will","It's said to be the latest high-end product developed by the DL. Once equipped, it allows the operator to enhance their combat abilities with the flick of a finger!"],["Will","All the various factions on Milkhama are searching for it. If we get our hands on it, or even gather some intel, we could sell it on the black market for a fortune that would set us up for life!"],["","Will grew loud and animated as he described the item, even drowning out the noise in the bar. Meanwhile, Meritus kept a stern face, then burst into sudden laughter."],["Meritus","Puhahaha! How did a fool like you manage to get by until now? Not a day goes by in this dump without some moron claiming to have made some game-changing discovery!"],["Meritus","Only those guys Ridge and Egbert would care... Rumors can't fill your stomach. And something about \"treasure\"...? Hahahaha..."],["Will","Huh? It's... like that, huh...?"],["","After realizing he was being mocked, Will awkwardly scratched his head, seeming a bit embarrassed. Just as he was about to step back, a nervous mercenary hurriedly approached Meritus with a phone in hand."],["","Meritus was initially fiddling with the fried chicken in his hand while having his underling hold the phone to his ear. After a few words, his expression suddenly changed, and he grabbed the phone, knocking over his beloved fast food."],["","Sensing the situation was off, Will tactfully got up to leave. But just as he turned around, Meritus suddenly called out to him from behind."],["Meritus","Stop!"],["Will","Uh... Me, boss?"],["Meritus","Kid... where'd you get that info from?"],["","Will turned around and found Meritus staring at him intently."],["Will","Boss... are you talking about this \"treasure\"?"],["Will","You just said it yourself, it's just a rumor. It's just this \"treasure\" has been coming up more and more lately, so..."],["Meritus","...Just now, our contact specifically reached out to me... He told me that our new employer is also interested in this so-called \"treasure\"..."],["Will","Our... new employer? Oh, Cross, the renowned \"philanthropic entrepreneur\" who sponsored your new Terrorclaw, right?"],["Meritus","Cross—also the biggest intelligence broker on the entire frontier..."],["Meritus","Recently, there's a newcomer from who knows where, causing a stir on his turf... The news of this \"treasure\" came from there."],["Meritus","You came at just the right time, kid... We've got a big job to do!"],["","DL Border Base"],["","The cockpit hatch eased open, and Victoria hopped down lightly. The adjutant, who had been waiting on the lift for some time, stepped forward at once to take her gloves."],["Victoria's Adjutant","Lieutenant, you're finally back. Commander Ruark wants you to go to his office immediately."],["Victoria","Hmph, here we go again... I'm not going. Just say that my team encountered an unexpected situation on the way back and needs to rest on the spot, so we can't carry out his orders for now."],["Victoria's Adjutant","...Lieutenant, after all, Commander Ruark is the base commander. Ever since you were seconded to the border defense forces, your relationship with him has been quite tense. This could affect your career..."],["Victoria","\"Career\"? Look at this godforsaken place, broken and desolate. What kind of career can there be?"],["","At this point, Victoria's voice suddenly took on an icy edge. In recent days, the reprimands from headquarters' officers often surfaced in her mind at inopportune moments."],["","Due to the failure of the surprise operation against Vesper, the DLAF's offensive had to undergo emergency changes on the eve of battle. She was deemed a disgrace to the military who must be taught a lesson."],["","So she was transferred here. This broken, desolate border base filled with endless despair... and as a bonus, a proud and overbearing superior."],["Victoria","My adjutant... you must broaden your view. Don't be swayed by Ruark's brainwashing rhetoric. We must ultimately find a way back to the DLAF headquarters."],["","Victoria quickly walked away. She has always been someone who takes \"Forceful Execution\" as her life creed. Once she sets a goal, she'll spare no effort, paving her way back with one medal of merit at a time."],["Victoria's Adjutant","B-but Lieutenant, Commander Ruark is still our direct superior. You've repeatedly disobeyed orders recently, and he's quite dissatisfied. If he decides to punish you for all your offenses, the consequences might be..."],["","Victoria stared blankly into the adjutant's eyes, and the hangar fell silent."],["Victoria","Do as I say, understand?"],["Victoria's Adjutant","...Yes."],["","Victoria turned to leave, but suddenly heard the sound of a mechanical door opening. She instantly had a bad feeling, and saw a figure slowly emerging from the stairs."],["","The two exchanged glances from a distance. The newcomer's eyes showed a hint of mockery the moment they saw Victoria."],["Ruark","What a coincidence, Lieutenant Victoria. It's not easy to meet someone as busy as you."],["","Victoria didn't speak, her gaze growing sharper. She slowly raised her hand in a salute."],["Ruark","Heh, so, on this mission, did you uncover the truth you've been desperately seeking? What rotting flesh is attracting those buzzing flies everywhere? Have you got rid of them? I assume there'll be no future troubles."],["Victoria","I have some leads, sir. Recently, defense outposts across the border have been frequently harassed by mercenary forces. They're all searching for something codenamed \"treasure\"."],["Ruark","Oh? What is that?"],["Victoria","...We're still unsure. I need more time..."],["Ruark","Heh, more time? Five violations and you still haven't uncovered the truth. How many more chances do you need from me?"],["","As Ruark's sarcasm intensified, Victoria clenched her fists."],["Victoria","Violations? Sir, I don't recall any of my sorties violating base regulations."],["Victoria","Recently, the base has been receiving frequent distress signals from various outposts. As a member of the border defense forces, it is my responsibility and obligation to respond promptly to these signals."],["Ruark","As a member of the border defense forces, you shouldn't formulate a rescue plan on your own. You should report the real-time battle situation to me first, then act according to my orders."],["Victoria","Act according to your orders? Ha, by the time you, sir, slowly finish analyzing the situation and dispatch us for support, those mercenaries will have already ransacked the outpost."],["Ruark","Victoria, watch your attitude! I'm your commanding officer. You are currently in serious violation of regulations. I don't want our next conversation to be at your suspension hearing!"],["Victoria","......"],["","Sparks flew in the space between them. Victoria's face was cold, and her voice involuntarily lowered."],["Victoria","...You can't do this, sir. The recent movements of the mercenaries are clearly suspicious. They are probing our bases, and there might be a larger conspiracy behind this. If I don't find out..."],["Ruark","Hmph, I know your family holds some weight within the DLAF... But how confident must you be to think you're irreplaceable? The distress signal can be heard by more than just you, Lieutenant!"],["Ruark","Headquarters sent you here to learn how to become a true DLAF soldier—not to act recklessly and continue making those foolish mistakes!"],["","Ruark's voice boomed like thunder, and Victoria clenched her fists tightly, even faintly feeling the vibrations from the ground. Just then, red lights flashed in the hangar, alarms blared, and the piercing wail crashed into Victoria's mind, relentlessly assaulting her sanity."],["DL Soldier","Commander! An unidentified mercenary force is rapidly approaching the base! Surveillance information is being relayed to all mobile terminals in the base! Requesting immediate entry to defensive combat status!"],["Ruark","Heh."],["","Ruark gave a mirthless smile, his mouth twitching as his gaze on Victoria grew ever more venomous."],["Ruark","I think I may have been wrong, Lieutenant. You're turning out to be far more useful than I thought."],["Ruark","Prove it to me. Prove that without you, those mercenaries will rush in and destroy us... As a member of the border defense force, you will protect them, won't you?"],["Victoria","......"],["","Victoria's Adjutant quickly checked the terminal's message logs. In the surveillance footage, a massive, motley wave of STs was approaching from afar. She swiftly scrolled through the screen and identified several memorable models that had appeared in the warrant."],["Victoria's Adjutant","This is bad—it's Meritus's team! Sir, the lieutenant's STs haven't had a chance to resupply. If we face Meritus like this—"],["Victoria","Shut up."],["Victoria's Adjutant","Lieutenant..."],["","The adjutant looked anxious, but her superior stood before her rigid and resolute, without as much as a twitch of her eyebrows."],["Victoria","I will prove it to you, sir, I promise."]],"468273301":[["","Border Base Military Prison"],["","The soldiers clapped and jeered at the defeated mercs, urging them on as they obediently marched into the prison."],["DL Soldier","Line up, single file! Don't try anything! This is the border base. Anyone resisting will be considered an enemy combatant and executed on the spot!"],["","Two lines of armed soldiers stood in the corridor, coldly watching the mercenaries file past. At the end of the line, a soldier was relentlessly driving them forward."],["","Will was jostled to the front of the crowd. Cold sweat streamed down his face and side, his expression frozen as he stared unblinkingly at the final cell where they'd be locked up."],["Meritus","Hey, are you scared, kid? Looks like ya can't even walk straight!"],["","The mercenaries laughed heartily, showing no sadness or tension about their impending imprisonment. The DL soldiers had to bang on the walls to silence the rabble."],["Will","N-no... I'm fine, I..."],["???","Halt."],["","Victoria intercepted the team. She had just come from the infirmary, wearing a tactical vest. Both of her arms were wrapped in bandages with faint traces of blood seeping through."],["DL Soldier","Everyone stop!"],["DL Soldier","Lieutenant, any orders?"],["Victoria","Bring him over."],["","Victoria pointed at Will."],["DL Soldier","Yes, Lieutenant."],["","A crack appeared on Will's stiff face as he instinctively looked at his boss beside him. Meritus remained calm and even nudged Will's shoulder, whispering something to him in a very low voice."],["Meritus","Just going through the motions. Don't be nervous, kid."],["","Will looked at Meritus with some trepidation, watching the only person who might have offered him protection drift further and further from reach, as soldiers escorted him into an adjacent interrogation room."],["","Without any time for mental preparation, he was quickly secured to a chair in the room. At first, passing companions would make funny faces at him through the glass partition, but soon Victoria pulled down the blinds."],["","Will swallowed hard, nervously staring at a small stain on the table in front of him."],["Victoria","Name."],["Will","Will Sander!!"],["Victoria","Are you trying to challenge me? Don't be so loud, just answer in a normal volume."],["Will","...G-Got it."],["Victoria","I'm Victoria, rank lieutenant. The team that subdued all of you outside the base today was led by me. You haven't forgotten, have you?"],["Will","I-It was you..."],["Victoria","Yes, it was me. I don't want to go through those tedious and lengthy formalities, so now tell me honestly the purpose of your attack on the base, and whether there are any other accomplices."],["","Victoria swiftly drew a saber and held it against Will's neck, raising an eyebrow with a hunter's expression."],["Victoria","I'll give you five seconds to speak. If you don't give me the answer I want in five seconds, this blade will end you."],["Will","N-no, I can't betray my comrades..."],["Victoria","Hmph, comrades? Do you mercs really consider each other \"comrades\"? Believe it or not, if I kill you here, the next one who comes in will see you lying there and give it up without hesitation."],["Will","No, no, wait..."],["Victoria","Five—"],["Will","Wait!! Let's discuss this again! There must be another way..."],["Victoria","Four—"],["Will","You're an officer, you can't just kill people..."],["Victoria","Three—"],["Will","I cannot betray..."],["Victoria","Two—"],["","Will felt a momentary chill on the side of his neck, followed by a lingering sting. Victoria's blade traced a line of blood along his neck, and terror rushed out of his body through that line."],["Victoria","One—!"],["Will","We're here for the \"treasure\"—!!"],["Victoria","... Hmph, just as expected."],["Will","..."],["","Will gasped for breath, drenched in sweat and trembling like a leaf. After uttering that incredibly mournful sentence, he fell into a soul-crushing silence."],["Victoria","... Well done, Will Sander."],["","Victoria withdrew her sword and slowly sat back down across from Will."],["Victoria","Your statement has gotten us off to a good start. Now, please continue. On my word as a soldier, as long as you cooperate, I will definitely strive to get you a reduced sentence."],["Victoria","Attacking a border base is a very serious crime, punishable by up to life imprisonment depending on the severity. Don't you want a second chance?"],["Will","...Life imprisonment?"],["Victoria","Of course. That means if you choose to remain silent, there are only two outcomes left: you sit in prison until you breathe your last, or I thrust this blade straight through your throat. Make your choice—you have three seconds."],["Will","......"],["Will","......"],["Will","\"Treasure\"... We came for it."],["Victoria","Don't repeat yourself. Tell me everything you know."],["Will","They all say the \"treasure\" is a good thing, that obtaining it grants the power to rival the two major forces..."],["Victoria","How is that possible? Who said that? Do you really believe such an outrageous rumor? You'd go as far to provoke the military based on gossip?"],["Will","It was the Sand Whale, the Sand Whale said it. All I know is that he's a mysterious information dealer with influence second only to Cross, often serving as a consultant to major underground forces."],["Will","He's got connections. People say if the Sand Whale reveals a way to make big money and you don't follow it, you'll end up being the only one left poor."],["Will","In a world where information stretches as endlessly as desert sand, he's the rare whale that navigates it effortlessly, devouring vast tracts, filtering out the noise, identifying the most valuable secrets... That's why when he announced news of a \"treasure,\" it sent everyone into a frenzy."],["Will","Even Cross... he's always been wary of him. Learning of the hunt for the \"treasure,\" he threw himself into it, determined to claim it first... So now all kinds of mercenaries are searching for it, like men possessed."],["Victoria","...Did that Sand Whale reveal anything more? What's the nature of this \"treasure\"?"],["Will","It's... some kind of computing device. It's said that Obsidian was also involved in its development..."],["","Will spoke while intently observing Victoria's expression. However, Victoria remained unfazed."],["Will","It is intricately linked to a technology called the \"Bionic Intelligence Frame,\" which is said to be someone's \"Legacy\"..."],["","Victoria's expression changed, and she leaned forward to grab Will by the collar."],["Victoria","What did you say?!"],["","Knock, knock, knock—the door of the interrogation room was knocked on."],["Victoria's Adjutant","Lieutenant, Commander Ruark is calling, stating that there is an extremely urgent order to be issued. Please answer as soon as possible."],["Victoria","Damn, now?!"],["","Victoria glanced at Will and quickly walked to the door to take the call."],["Victoria","Commander Ruark, the interrogation is underway. Would you like to come and personally oversee it?"],["Ruark","Your voice remains firm, Lieutenant. I'm calling to inform you of a development: the mercenaries are to be released on bail, effective immediately. You've just returned from battle; take time to rest."],["Victoria","So soon?! Under whose name was the bail posted?"],["Ruark","Lieutenant, I'm here to deliver a notification, not to answer your questions. Execute the order immediately; we no longer have a legitimate reason to detain them."],["Victoria","No! Sir, I've already extracted some crucial information. If we continue the investigation, we can definitely uncover who's behind this. If we let them go now, these mercenaries won't abide by the bail terms—"],["Ruark","Continue the investigation? You've violated protocol five times before and still haven't found the supposed \"mastermind.\" Now you want the entire base to bear the risk of breaking the law and join your antics?"],["Victoria","Are you—"],["Ruark","Release them immediately, don't give them a chance to sue us! Look at your comrades around you—they don't have someone at headquarters who can speak for them like you do."],["","Beep-beep-beep..."],["Victoria","Who bought you off?"],["","Victoria couldn't finish her sentence. She looked grim, clutching the communicator tightly. Victoria took several deep breaths at the door before returning to the interrogation room, where Will watched her anxiously yet expectantly."],["Victoria","What else do you know about the \"Sand Whale\"?"],["Will","The Sand Whale is notoriously elusive—how could someone like me know anything about a guy like that... But L-Lieutenant, did I just hear \"bail\"...? Did Boss Cross come to save us?!"],["","Victoria's eyebrows twitch."],["Victoria","...Boss? So you're his subordinates?"],["Will","..."],["","Will belatedly realized he must have said something wrong and looked at Victoria with unusual nervousness, covering his mouth. However, she suddenly raised the corners of her mouth."],["Victoria","Heh, if he's the biggest information broker in the borderlands, he should have some information about Sand Whale, shouldn't he?"],["","On the desert highway, Meritus's ST units sped by one after another, kicking up clouds of yellow sand."],["Meritus","Come on you slackers! Give it all you've got! We reach the Samba Tavern before dark, every single one of us! Those who fall behind share the bill!"],["","Laughter echoed continuously through the communication channel as Meritus burst into a hearty chuckle, cranking the ST's power output to the max and singing from the depths of his diaphragm."],["","His singing was as bold as his appearance, and surprisingly, many in the group knew the song too. For a moment, the channel was filled with a chorus of voices."],["Mercenary B","Wait, boss, there's a car stopped up ahead!"],["Meritus","What is it? With such a big formation, they still won't move aside? Are they looking for trouble?"],["Mercenary B","They have no intention of making way, boss. Could they be waiting for us on purpose? Did that girl change her mind?"],["Mercenary A","Tch... Is there anyone besides Sand Whale who'd disrespect Cross in this territory? Wait, could that be them in that car?"],["Meritus","Stop guessing. Let's go over and see what's going on. All of you, stay alert. If anything seems off, shoot first, ask questions later!"],["","At the end of the road, a black sedan was parked sideways. Meritus came to a sudden stop in front of it. The tightly closed car window slowly rolled down, revealing an aloof and composed man in a crisp suit, unfazed even when facing an ST several times his size."],["???","Meritus?"],["Meritus","It's me... Who are you? What do you want?"],["???","You don't need to know who I am. Just remember—the only reason you've escaped punishment because someone is covering for you."],["Meritus","Oh... I see, you're with \"that officer.\""],["???","...Recently, your behavior has been problematic. Sooner or later, you'll drag my superior down with you. That wasn't part of the deal."],["Meritus","Tsk, are you lecturing us, blaming us for what other mercs have done?"],["???","There's no difference. You're all subordinates of Cross, and if someone eventually digs deeper into your bail records, they might discover the relationship between him and my superior."],["???","So, for the sake of long-term interests, please keep a low profile for the time being."],["Meritus","Tsk, tsk... do you want me to repeat that to Mr. Cross?"],["???","Excuse me. This is the third time I've conveyed this directive from my superior. Perhaps my words carry little weight, which is why they've had little effect. Perhaps if Mr. Cross handles this issue himself, we'll be able to avoid any future difficulties."],["Meritus","......"],["","The black car sped away in the opposite direction of the Meritus team, leaving a bunch of metal hulks in its exhaust."],["Mercenary B","Hey, boss, he's really arrogant—not afraid of us at all!"],["Meritus","His boss works with ours—what's there for him to be afraid of?"],["Mercenary B","But hey, didn't you try to use Mr. Cross's name to try and scare him?"],["Meritus","Tch, if Cross's name doesn't carry much weight him them, that's not my problem."],["Meritus","Speaking of scary, my stomach growls are getting out of control! Let's hurry back and eat. We can talk hash it out after we're full."],["","The Samba Tavern is bustling with activity once again. Today's failed base trip hasn't dampened the mercs' lust for life in the slightest."],["","Will struggled to squeeze out of the swaying crowd, and after rejecting countless bottles and glasses, he arrived at the back door of the tavern."],["","He glanced around the entire tavern. With everyone immersed in the revelry of alcohol and music, no one noticed his actions."],["","Will opened the door and walked out. A misty drizzle was falling outside, with neon lights softly diffused in the rain."],["","He took a deep breath of the cool air outside, letting the lightness fill his lungs again. Then he cupped his hands, lit a cigarette, and the faint glow illuminated his deep-set eyes."],["???","Nice smoke, friend. Can I have one too?"],["","Will paused, flicking the cigarette between his fingers as he turned around. A passing man had somehow appeared behind him."],["Will","No problem—"],["","Will opened the cigarette case, finding it empty. He gave an apologetic smile."],["Will","Sorry, I just lit the last one. Come with me, I'll buy another pack."],["","The two left the tavern's back alley one after the other. The rain was like a fine mist, slowly forming transparent droplets on their hair."],["???","The bait has been set; the fish will soon take the hook."],["???","......"],["???","Yes. But Sand Whale, if the DL takes strong measures against you without negotiation, what should we do?"],["Sand Whale","Wouldn't that be exactly what we want? If you want to blend into a pack of wolves, you must first learn to play the part of a sheep."],["Sand Whale's Underling","...I understand. So what should I do next?"],["Sand Whale","This operation has revealed some interesting insider information to me, which might serve as a safeguard... You should approach Frank's group in my name."],["Sand Whale's Underling","Frank? He's Cross's loyal dog. He probably won't listen to \"Sand Whale.\""],["Sand Whale","Loyal dog? Haha, even you can misjudge people sometimes."],["Sand Whale","Just a stray dog adept at sniffing out advantage. Loyalty rests on self-interest—it only exists where there's advantage. And now, his master's about to fall into a whole world of trouble."],["Sand Whale's Underling","...?"],["Sand Whale","Pass this message to Frank. We'll meet soon."]],"468277101":[["","DL Border Base"],["","Recently, Nathaniel Cross, a renowned entrepreneur in Thepia, was detained and investigated by local law enforcement for alleged tax fraud. The news immediately drew widespread attention from the markets and the public."],["","According to inside sources, the investigation into this case involves amounts going into the tens of millions and serious illegal activities such as concealing income and falsifying financial statements. Currently, relevant departments are conducting a comprehensive investigation into the enterprises under Cross's name, with detailed information pending disclosure."],["Victoria","That's the situation, Ma'at. The Sand Whale lead is key to unraveling the conspiracy behind the border unrest. I'll move on Cross first. Then we'll harpoon that whale straight out of the dunes."],["Victoria","Another thing, you'd better start looking into any internal leaks of \"Legacy\" secrets. I have a feeling this matter won't be that simple."],["Ma'at","......"],["Victoria","Ma'at? What's your response?"],["Ma'at","In fact, Lieutenant Victoria, I would advise you to suspend the plan."],["Victoria","What do you mean? Didn't you understand what I just said? This series of disturbances at the border was incited by the Sand Whale using the \"treasure\" as a lure. Even if he's not the mastermind, he's definitely connected to them."],["Ma'at","Yes, but you don't need to go to such lengths..."],["Victoria","Not take it seriously? Ma'at, that Sand Whale mentioned the Legacy, which is one of the highest-level secrets of the DL. He definitely knows something and wants to use mercenaries to seize the Legacy to harm us."],["Ma'at","Calm down, Lieutenant Victoria. I understand your concerns, but please trust that we have always maintained the upper hand."],["","On the other end of the line, Ma'at let out a soft sigh."],["Ma'at","The Legacy has already drawn the attention of many factions, and its existence is no longer a top secret. As an information broker, it's not surprising that the Sand Whale learned about it."],["Ma'at","He understands the value of Legacy and wants to claim it for himself—that much is obvious. But if that's his only purpose, then we need not worry."],["Victoria","Need not worry?! Ma'at—"],["Ma'at","The Legacy is now under tight protection. No one is taking it anywhere."],["Victoria","No protection is ever absolute. Even the strongest vault can be blasted to pieces. Only by completely eliminating those with covetous intentions can you protect what you want to safeguard."],["Victoria","Ma'at, do I really need to remind you of this?"],["Ma'at","You can rest assured, Lieutenant Victoria. Even if someone is foolish enough to reach for the Legacy, they'll soon find it utterly beyond their grasp."],["Victoria","Blind confidence will become your fatal weakness. I demand to speak with Lukmund..."],["Ma'at","You may not trust me, but you're a soldier too. Surely you trust that \"Super Pilot,\" right?"],["Victoria","...Her?! The Legacy is in her hands?!"],["","Victoria's flushed face was full of shifting emotions."],["","Super Pilot... this codename is used exclusively within the DLAF to refer to that one and only pilot."],["Victoria","Ada Diaz... Has she also made a move...?"],["","After the shock, a hint of melancholy appeared on Victoria's face... That's right, with her around, the Legacy is as good as secured, isn't it...?"],["","But for Victoria herself, she finally uncovered a crucial clue. Continuing the investigation will surely lead her to that Sand Whale, and then she can settle the recent border unrest—a significant achievement."],["","The future of returning to the core circle is already beckoning her. With her career in the military at stake—how could she stop now?"],["Victoria","I believe the sudden actions of the border mercenaries should not be underestimated. There might be something behind this—"],["Ma'at","The border unrest is currently under the control of the DLAF. Until the Sand Whale reveals his intentions, there is no need to launch overt actions that might alert him. We need to bide our time."],["Victoria","But Ma'at..."],["Ma'at","That's all, Lieutenant Victoria. I have an urgent matter to attend to. Returning to base."],["","The other side quickly hung up. Victoria took a deep breath, and finally, with a frown of irritation, closed her eyes."],["","For Ma'at, this was just a trivial incident, but for her, it was an important opportunity to establish merit... Is she really willing to give it up like this?"],["","The TV continued to broadcast news of Cross's arrest. Victoria listened for two minutes, and suddenly the communicator rang again. She glanced at the name on the screen and answered."],["Victoria","Is the matter settled?"],["Victoria's Informant","The paperwork for Cross's detention has just been completed. You can visit him in two days at the earliest, but this is your only chance, so make the most of it."],["Victoria","Isn't that rushing things? His business empire is so vast, it's going to take quite some time to get through everything, isn't it?"],["Victoria's Informant","It's not that simple. Cross has always been meticulous in his actions and is well-versed in dealing with us. We've been watching him for a long time and only managed to catch a small slip-up. We originally planned to hit him with multiple charges to catch him off guard."],["Victoria's Informant","This time, we decided to take action because you suggested he might have improper financial dealings with high-ranking military officials. But if we can't find more evidence..."],["Victoria","Heh."],["","Victoria laughed at the words, her sarcasm evident."],["Victoria","Keep digging deeper, Annie, you won't be disappointed. I've reviewed nearly two years of files in the base archives, and those unsolved major cases are all related to Cross - letting those major criminals leave the base safely couldn't have happened without Ruark's special pass."],["Victoria","If you can find any records of their dealings, you'd be doing me a big favor."],["Victoria's Informant","Sigh, let's hope so. If we can completely eliminate the cancer that is Cross, these years wouldn't have been in vain. See you, Victoria."],["Sand Whale","Then, a toast to our brand new future, Mr. Frank."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","......"],["","Sand Whale raised his champagne glass, while Frank sat motionless across from him. The dozen or so strong men surrounding Frank also chose to remain silent before the boss spoke. The private room was suddenly enveloped in an eerie serenity."],["","Sand Whale smiled. There was no one behind him, yet he remained composed, slowly finished the drink, and gently placed the glass on the coffee table in front of him."],["Sand Whale","I thought we had reached an agreement—work with me, and I will fully support you in becoming the new leader of the Cross Group. Regardless of Cross's ultimate fate, he will no longer have a chance to rise again."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","...Sand Whale."],["Sand Whale","Please."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","Answer me an important question first."],["Sand Whale","Please."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","This trouble with Cross—was it you?"],["Sand Whale","...Heh, I thought it was a common understanding in our line of work not to involve the military and police—"],["Cross's Loyal Dog","Answer me, was it you?"],["","The strong men stared intently, and Sand Whale immediately felt as if he was being aimed at by a dozen sniper rifles. But he made an unexpected move—he spread his arms and leaned back on the sofa completely relaxed."],["Sand Whale","Absolutely not. The tax bureau and Cross have been at odds for a long time. You know how aggressive Cross's recent actions have been. He slipped up, gave them exactly what they needed, and now they'll bury him with it."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","You moved the moment he got into trouble. Are you really going to sit there and say this has nothing to do with you?"],["Sand Whale","Of course. But I know an opportunity when I see one... And if I see one, so too must others. Wouldn't you agree, Mr. Frank?"],["Cross's Loyal Dog","......"],["Sand Whale","Haha, see, if I don't make a move, someone else will. The prize left behind by the \"Great Snakehead\" is quite tempting. Do you want to hand it over to strangers, or claim it for yourself?"],["Cross's Loyal Dog","...Don't lump me in with your sort."],["Sand Whale","Come on, if we don't make a move, Cross's assets will be divided by others sooner or later. By the time he gets out, you'll already be someone else's dog."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","You—!"],["Sand Whale","But it's different with me here. I can help you. Once you become the new head of the Cross Group, you can do whatever you want."],["Sand Whale","You could even... wait until Cross is released and then return all his assets. I'm sure it would mean a lot to him."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","..."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","What are the terms?"],["Sand Whale","Hahaha, I knew we were on the same page, Mr. Frank. I know what you're really thinking..."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","Cut the crap. I'm getting tired of this."],["Sand Whale","The \"treasure.\" Just help me find it—that's all I need. Cross's assets should satisfy you for now. As for the object I seek—that I won't be sharing."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","......"],["Cross's Loyal Dog","Heh heh..."],["","Frank was silent for a moment before suddenly chuckling softly. The cold air that had solidified between him and Sand Whale seemed to gradually ripple."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","So it's actually real... Sand Whale, that thing actually exists? I thought it was just more of your smoke and mirrors, something to..."],["","He paused, spreading his hands as if searching for the right words."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","To cover up your true intentions. It's as though you wanted to dig a pit for my boss, push him in, and then loot his assets."],["Sand Whale","You've got a good sense of humor. Unfortunately, your boss isn't the type to jump into a pit someone else dug—he usually does it himself."],["Sand Whale","But no, the \"treasure\" really exists. But you know my ways. Even if the whole world were to covet my possessions—what's mine is mine."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","......"],["","Frank and Sand Whale exchanged glances, then sat for a while, silently assessing the situation."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","You haven't fully earned my trust, Sand Whale, but for the greater good, we can cooperate."],["Sand Whale","You're a natural leader, Mr. Frank, much better than that hypocrite Cross—"],["Cross's Loyal Dog","But first, you need to help me deal with someone."],["Sand Whale","So I'm already being put to work, huh? Uh... I mean, who?"],["Cross's Loyal Dog","Cross's connections in the border defense forces."],["Cross's Loyal Dog","You're right, Sand Whale. Everyone wants a piece of this pie, even if the other party is wearing an official hat. My background is limited, so I can't confront him head-on. But if you help me deal with him, we can immediately get to work."],["","Sand Whale was taken aback, then smiled and clapped his hands."],["Sand Whale","What a coincidence, Mr. Frank. I was just thinking of having a good chat with that \"officer.\""],["","Sand Whale walked out of the hotel and lit another cigarette, the flame illuminating the lingering amusement in his eyes."],["","He blew out a series of smoke rings, humming an unknown tune, as he stepped into the dark, narrow alley."],["","He stopped at a crossroads, the ashes from his cigarette falling like snowflakes. At this moment, only the starlight above could help him discern his position, as four long roads stretched from his feet into the unknown darkness."],["","A gust of wind suddenly came from behind his head. Sand Whale, having anticipated it, quickly ducked and started running."],["???","Damn, he saw us—chase him!"],["","Sand Whale ran into an alley, but it was not easy to traverse, filled with residents' clutter. He had to remove obstacles as he made his way through."],["","The young pursuer was strong and agile, quickly climbing onto the eaves and moving unhindered. He soon ran ahead and pounced down, pinning him to the ground."],["Sand Whale","Hey! Friend, I remember you, Cross's bodyguard, Egbert, right? Let's talk this out, let's talk this out—"],["Egbert","What's there to talk about?! I just overheard you trying to turn my boss's subordinates against him while he's away!"],["","Sand Whale was somewhat surprised, initially thinking it was an old enemy seeking revenge, but it turned out to be an impatient hothead."],["Sand Whale","You misunderstood, Mr. Frank and I..."],["Egbert","Stop talking, my work principles don't allow such things to happen. Arguing is useless—"],["","Click—Sand Whale heard the sound of a safety catch being pulled behind him and immediately sped up his speech."],["Sand Whale","Everything is to rescue Mr. Cross!"],["Egbert","What did you say?!"],["Sand Whale","Everything is for Mr. Cross! I plan to contact that 'Officer' to find a way to bail out Mr. Cross first, and then slowly resolve the tax crisis..."],["Egbert","But that's not what you said earlier. You incited Frank to annex my boss's property!"],["Sand Whale","Frank had issues to begin with, he would have replaced Cross without me—you heard it too, he wants to use me to smooth out his troubles before he takes over. I just want to use him to get in touch with that \"officer\"."],["Egbert","......"],["","Egbert was a bit hesitant, he only heard a rough idea earlier and didn't fully know the details. Did he really misunderstand?"],["Sand Whale","Trust me this once, my friend, Mr. Cross is waiting for us to make a move and get him out."],["Egbert","I... I have a gun in my hand, so don't try any tricks!"],["Sand Whale","Of course, who dares to race against a gun? Friend, can we make a deal and let me get up first? I'm almost suffocating here... Let me get up and tell you the truth. If you find anything wrong, you can take action anytime."],["","Sand Whale waited for a while, but no reply came. Just as he prepared to speak again, he suddenly felt a lightness on his body as he was hauled up to his feet."],["Sand Whale","Thank you, friend."],["Egbert","Don't thank me yet, I still have questions..."],["","Thud! With a muffled sound, Sand Whale headbutted with lightning speed, and while Egbert was seeing stars, he quickly scrambled onto the rooftop and made a swift escape."],["Egbert","That... bastard...!"],["Egbert","Attention everyone! He's heading east. I'm synchronizing the coordinates right now. Surround him!"],["","Sand Whale was running at full speed across the rooftops. On the distant horizon, the fiery dawn was slowly dispelling the surrounding darkness. He was in euphoria, whistling as he ran."],["","His destination was an abandoned steel mill, where he had a reserved ST. Once he got on the ST, not even Egbert could catch up with him."],["","However, when Sand Whale sat in the cockpit, his ears perked up keenly, and the vibrations coming from all directions announced that he was surrounded."],["Sand Whale","Oh dear, it seems today's morning exercise is quite intense."],["","Sand Whale smiled as he pulled the lever, his eyes full of eagerness to try."]],"468277301":[["","Sand Whale piloted the ST to swiftly leave the battlefield. Having just won a brawl, he was in high spirits, tapping his fingers on the lever to the rhythm of a certain song."],["","As he passed the fork in the road leading home, he hesitated for a moment, then sped off in the opposite direction."],["","Sand Whale booked a room at a new hotel, paying special attention to the location of the emergency exit as he went upstairs. The room was at the end of the hallway, making it convenient for him to evacuate the building as quickly as possible in case of an emergency."],["","He opened the door and walked in. He planned to reward himself with a hearty brunch and then take a nap to replenish the energy he lost last night."],["","A click. Sand Whale paused, sighed, and slowly raised his two hands, turning around."],["Sand Whale","Tsk, a curse on all the handgun manufacturers..."],["???","Huh? This is the one who tricked you? He just looks like some random guy...."],["","Just as Sand Whale was about to speak, he heard the sound of glass shattering behind him. Someone climbed in from outside, still panting."],["Egbert","Don't underestimate him. He's full of lies; you can't believe a word he says."],["???","Then don't let him speak—goodbye, \"random guy\"!"],["Sand Whale","Sand Whale—my name is Sand Whale—Ridgewald. Kill me and the \"treasure\" will be lost to you forever."],["Egbert","What?! You know Ridge too?!"],["Ridgewald","Sand Whale? ...Sounds familiar. Real familiar."],["","With a troubled expression, Ridgewald tapped her head with her free hand. Suddenly, she had an epiphany."],["Ridgewald","It's you!"],["Egbert","Who? You know him too?"],["Ridgewald","I don't know him. When we decided to work with the Information Dealer to find the \"treasure,\" I heard Eller mention him."],["Ridgewald","Cross is the head of the information market and likes to play the philanthropist. Sand Whale's the runner-up, like some second uncle hiding in the shadows. You don't remember?"],["Egbert","Oh, then... when you were chatting Meritus was taking a nap. I ended up sitting down next to him and dozed off too..."],["Ridgewald","I knew I couldn't rely on you guys."],["Sand Whale","Wait a minute, \"second uncle\"? What'd I do to earn such a strange nickname?"],["Ridgewald","Maybe it's because with Cross around, you're always second best, yet your personal style is too self-centered... Did you know there's a forum on the net where merc go specifically to complain about you?"],["Sand Whale","Although I've made some achievements in intelligence work, I must admit that even the best intelligence officer has knowledge gaps..."],["Ridgewald","You really don't care about what others think of you, do you? So you never bothered to find out... But there's no need to know anyway. When we tried to find information about you for collaboration, we spent a whole day and found nothing useful."],["Ridgewald","You don't show up often, and they don't have many ways to know the real you, so all they can do is give you vague labels: \"powerful,\" \"mysterious,\" \"flexible,\" \"abstract\"..."],["Sand Whale","If you hadn't mentioned that last word, I would have already created a new account to join my fan club."],["Ridgewald","Ha! But today, now, you finally appear before us—with your unremarkable appearance and unremarkable skills—standing right there."],["Sand Whale","...I'm truly sorry to shatter your illusions, Miss Ridgewald, but if you're willing to learn more about me..."],["","Ridgewald rolled her eyes impatiently, then suddenly moved closer to Sand Whale, making an aiming gesture. Sand Whale immediately fell silent, awkwardly smiling."],["Sand Whale","Alright, perhaps it's better to discuss something more meaningful now, like how you managed to find me this time...?"],["","Egbert let out a cold laugh, smugly pulling a terminal from his pocket, which displayed the real-time location of Sand Whale on the screen."],["Sand Whale","Ah... I see, so you placed a tracking device on me back then."],["Egbert","Good thing I had this trick up my sleeve, or you would have gotten away!"],["Sand Whale","Alright, alright, alright, since it's come to this, let's speak frankly. I know what you want, and I happen to be able to provide it. How about teaming up?"],["Egbert","Nonsense, we won't be fooled by you again. Ridge, shoot."],["Sand Whale","Really? If you kill me, you'll be getting further and further away from the \"treasure.\""],["Ridgewald","......"],["Egbert","Ridge?"],["Ridgewald","We really can't kill him—at least not for now. Egbert, this guy knows more about the \"treasure\" than Cross does. Now that something has happened to Cross, we really need a new source of intel."],["Sand Whale","It's an honor to have your approval, Miss Ridgewald."],["Egbert","Are you really interested in that so-called \"treasure\"? He's a wily one... how can we trust what he says?"],["Ridgewald","It don't care, he's got me intrigued! So, Sand Whale, speak. As long as you keep me interested, I won't pull the trigger."],["","Sand Whale chuckled, no longer assuming a defensive posture, but instead slowly walked to the bar under the muzzle of Ridgewald's gun, poured himself a glass of water, and drank it in one gulp."],["Sand Whale","Regarding the \"treasure,\" everything you know is information I carefully considered before the leak. My goal is simple: to use the mercenaries scattered across the island to pinpoint its exact location."],["Ridgewald","So you don't know where that thing is either? Then how can we work together—?"],["Sand Whale","It is the pinnacle of the DL's technology, always under tight protection. But you know the island hasn't been peaceful lately, with Vesper stirring up a storm on the East Island. Whether it is still in the DL's hands is uncertain."],["Sand Whale","Recently, there's been some news from other parts of the island, but on the DL side remains as impregnable as ever... Don't you think it's worth exploring?"],["Ridgewald","No wonder Cross has been urging us to find a way to strike the DLAF... He must also suspect that the \"treasure\" is hidden by the DL."],["Sand Whale","His method is inefficient. The fastest approach is to directly contact higher-ups within the DL."],["Ridgewald","That's strange. Isn't Cross quite close with the commander at the border base? Why aren't they sharing this information...? Could it be that the officer knows nothing at all?"],["Sand Whale","We shouldn't rule out this possibility just yet. But we must also consider another possibility—the officer might actually be unaware that Cross is searching for the \"treasure\"... Cross might be deliberately concealing his actions."],["Egbert","You say he doesn't know, but did the officer tell you that?"],["Sand Whale","Given Cross's caution and greed, if he shares information about the \"treasure\" with Ruark, even if he finds the \"treasure\" in the end, he would have to make concessions."],["Sand Whale","With what you know about him, do you think he would be such a generous person?"],["Ridgewald","......"],["Egbert","......"],["","Ridgewald and Egbert exchanged a glance, recalling the day they received sponsorship from Cross."],["","Even though it was agreed that the sponsored ST should be prepared to fit their piloting habits, the model was changed at the last minute due to the \"company's recent budget constraints.\""],["","While Meritus laughed heartily, patting Dreadtalon without a care, Eller's expression changed immediately."],["Ridgewald","...Your guess is not without merit. So, what then? What can we do with this information?"],["Sand Whale","There are many interesting things we can do, Miss Ridgewald. I have a bargaining chip that none of you possess—knowledge of the \"treasure.\" And unlike Cross, I don't mind sharing it."],["Ridgewald","Do you want to collaborate with Ruark to find out the whereabouts of the \"treasure\"? Have you worked with him before?"],["Sand Whale","Not yet, but..."],["Ridgewald","I must pour some cold water on this. Sand Whale, Cross, and Ruark have been working together for a long time. You might not be able to get in."],["Sand Whale","Really? Then why does their partnership seem to be on the verge of collapse?"],["","Sand Whale looked at Egbert."],["Sand Whale","Do you remember what Frank said last night?"],["","Ridgewald also looks at Egbert."],["","Egbert met Ridgewald's gaze, and his heart instantly raced, sweating nervously."],["Egbert","R-Remember?"],["","——Remember? As if! He didn't even hear the whole thing!"],["Sand Whale","After Cross was imprisoned, Ruark attempted to take over the \"Legacy\" he left behind, but his position prevents him from directly doing so."],["Sand Whale","He needs a puppet, a powerful yet controlled puppet—this role is practically tailor-made for me."],["Ridgewald","Hmm..."],["Egbert","B-But..."],["","Egbert understands Ridgewald—he knows she has gradually come to accept Sand Whale's plan. But a faint voice in Egbert's heart whispers to him, putting him on guard, regardless of how reasonable Sand Whale's plan appears."],["","Sure enough, after a moment of silence, Ridgewald put down the gun."],["Ridgewald","I acknowledge your idea, Sand Whale. It's worth a try. Even if Ruark doesn't really know the whereabouts of this \"treasure,\" his identity can help us gather information... We can cooperate for now."],["Sand Whale","That's great, Miss Ridgewald. I happen to have something very important that I need your help with."],["Ridgewald","Let's hear it."],["Sand Whale","For this plan to be successfully implemented, we must first ensure one major premise—Cross will not interfere with Ruark's judgment."],["Sand Whale","They're still allies, so if Cross seeks Ruark's aid by offering to share the \"treasure\"... I can't guarantee one hundred percent that Ruark will choose me over him."],["Ridgewald","Tsk, so what do you want us to do? Take out Cross?"],["Egbert","No, no, Ridge, are you crazy? Killing someone in the police station's prison?"],["Sand Whale","Of course not, I just need you to shut him up."],["Ridgewald","So they weren't lying when they said you're abstract... Sand Whale, Cross is a normal person. Even if you shut his mouth and poison his vocal cords, he can still type and use hand gestures—"],["Sand Whale","What if we get him to agree to no longer contact Ruark?"],["Ridgewald","...Is that possible? Can you teach me some hypnosis techniques quickly?"],["Sand Whale","Heh. Cross, suddenly jailed—someone that careful has never taken a fall like this. At this sort of moment, even the slightest nudge will be enough to have him second-guessing... Who was it? Which of his people betrayed him...?"],["Sand Whale","I need his confidant imprisoned to do this, but time is tight. It's too late to persuade those stubborn ones. If we go with the backup plan, the candidate should at least be someone he recognizes as his own..."],["","Sand Whale looked at Ridgewald with a meaningful gaze."],["Ridgewald","...I can handle it."],["Sand Whale","Aha, you have great leadership potential. It's going to be a pleasure working with you..."],["Egbert","No way! Ridge, how can you just go along with his words and get yourself involved?"],["Ridgewald","Since we've decided to cooperate, why are you still being so hesitant over such a small matter?"],["Egbert","No, that won't do either! Ridge, you're still wanted by the DL. If you must go, I'll go in your place..."],["Ridgewald","Don't joke around. Who would think a wanted criminal would run into a prison themselves? If I disguise myself, no one will suspect a thing. You have a more crucial task—"],["Ridgewald","We can't fully trust him. You need to keep an eye on this guy. If you find out he's deceived us or is up to something outside..."],["","Ridgewald throws the gun in her hand to Egbert."],["Ridgewald","Use this gun to break his skull."],["","The police interrogation room. Victoria leans back in her chair, arms crossed with an impatient expression. The man sitting across from her, however, is at ease, continuously rubbing a teapot."],["Victoria","I will emphasize one last time—Cross, the evidence currently held by the tax bureau is enough to keep you in prison for decades. Now, make amends by confessing your trade with Ruark, and it will be your last chance for a reduced sentence."],["Cross","Let me emphasize one last time, Lieutenant Victoria, I am not aware of the matters you mentioned. The only connection between Commander Ruark and me might be the morning news—we often appear in reports on different topics."],["Cross","Additionally, if it's a tax issue, please have the tax office staff discuss it in detail with my legal team."],["Cross","Perhaps, Lieutenant, you are considering a transfer to the tax office, but I think it's best not to meddle in work unrelated to you until you obtain the proper qualifications... What do you think?"],["","Cross retaliated with an impenetrable defense, maintaining a faint smile on his face."],["Victoria","Heh."],["","Victoria sneered, opened the folder on the desk, and pulled out a few sheets of paper to place under Cross's eyes. These were copies of several files."],["Victoria","\"Logan Pierce,\" \"Jared Cole,\" \"Ethan Grayson,\" do you remember them?"],["Cross","Sorry, who...?"],["Victoria","A year ago, there was a heinous murder case at the Samba Tavern. The criminal clashed with undercover officers inside the tavern, resulting in five deaths and ten wounded."],["Victoria","Officer Kevin, who was investigating the case, eventually found the three murderers but lost his life during the pursuit."],["Cross","......"],["Victoria","And now, these three individuals have been released from prison and are employed at the mechanical factory under your name."],["","Cross remained expressionless, but Victoria heard a faint yet clear clinking sound—the teapot lid rattled because Cross's hand had just trembled."],["Victoria","Why? Because during the trial, crucial evidence went missing, leading to the case being thrown out. Coincidentally, they were being held in the base's military prison at that time."],["Cross","So, you think all of this is actually the result of a collusion between me and Commander Ruark? Haha, Lieutenant, your imagination is quite vivid."],["Cross","I apologize for such a misunderstanding, but my daily work is extremely busy, making it difficult to personally oversee the background check process of every employee under the company..."],["Victoria","No need to rush to clear your name, Cross. You wouldn't want to know what evidence I still hold. Can you really distance yourself from him after all your collusion?"],["Victoria","Heh... It's quite interesting, isn't it? The tax bureau has crossed paths with you many times before without gaining the upper hand. Yet this time, they've trapped you here, helpless... Do you want to know who tipped the scales?"],["","Cross's smile left his face; he placed the teapot on the table."],["Cross","Lieutenant Victoria, I know you're implying that Commander Ruark secretly manipulated things to get me imprisoned... but you're really mistaken. I don't know him, nor do we have any vested interests; he has no reason to harm me."],["Cross","As for the tax issues, I believe it's all a misunderstanding. Once the tax bureau uncovers the truth, they will naturally clear my name."],["","Victoria's expression was stern. She had already spent an hour here, and during this hour, no matter how she threatened or enticed, Cross remained unmoved. Continuing like this would only waste this precious opportunity."],["","What other conditions could sway Cross? Is she really going to let all her previous efforts go to waste this time?"],["Victoria","...Mr. Cross, perhaps you still believe you can be bailed out tomorrow or the day after, but I'm afraid you're going to be disappointed, because this time you will have no one to rely on..."],["Victoria's Informant","Victoria, the interrogation is over. Leave there immediately."],["","Suddenly, Annie's voice came through the headset. Victoria frowned and quickly walked to the corner, responding softly."],["Victoria","What's going on?"],["Victoria's Informant","Cross's secretary has come with a team of lawyers to visit. According to the rules, we can't stop them. Your interrogation this time can't be public—don't let them see you."],["Victoria","Damn it, what are the odds?"],["Victoria's Informant","Anyway, come out first, and we'll think of a way."],["","Victoria gave Cross a deep look, and the latter gave her a polite smile. Two seconds later, she reluctantly walked away, gritting her teeth."],["","After she left the interrogation room, Cross's smile faded, and his face was full of contemplation—until the door to the interrogation room was opened again."],["Cross","It's... you?"],["","Ridgewald gestured for him to be silent, intending to point at the surveillance to giving a hint to Cross, but after looking around, there wasn't a single surveillance camera."],["Ridgewald","Phew... there's actually no surveillance."],["","Ridgewald pulled out the chair opposite Cross and sat down unceremoniously, even propping her legs up on the table. The group of \"lawyers\" who followed her in stood behind her, looking slightly nervous and restrained."],["Ridgewald","Don't be surprised, boss. The group is in chaos right now, and I had no choice but to come—otherwise, how do you think a wanted criminal like me would just waltz into a prison?"],["Cross","What happened to the group? Where's Frank? Before I left, I specifically instructed him to stabilize the situation..."],["Ridgewald","Useless boss, someone wants to pull you down from that position—he's allied with Sand Whale, imprisoned Frank and the others, and now all your trusted aides are under surveillance."],["Cross","What?!"],["","Cross stood up in shock, his eyes filled with disbelief as he stared at Ridgewald."],["Ridgewald","Don't get excited, boss. The urgent task is to find a way to deal with Sand Whale and the one behind all this... To control your trusted aides in such a short time, the opponent must be someone who knows you well and has strong backing, right?"],["Cross","..."],["Ridgewald","Boss, have you figured out who it is?"],["Cross","…That's not something you need to worry about."],["Ridgewald","I'm only concerned about whether you can settle the commission for this period—so I have to get you out first."],["Ridgewald","But now we're facing a problem. The tax office is completely unyielding, and it's clear someone tipped them off to keep you locked up in prison. Innumerable pieces of evidence are piling up—they even rejected your bail application."],["","Cross's face was terrifyingly grim. With such actions, it's obvious who's plotting against him."],["Cross","Enough, you can't beat him."],["Ridgewald","Is it really necessary to go through all the trouble of fighting? It's just a matter of one bullet. But boss... we need to agree on the price first."],["","Cross shows a weary expression and pinches his brow, beginning to ponder."],["Cross","Do you know where he is? Do you know how many defense troops are on his turf?"],["Ridgewald","Tch..."],["Cross","You can't beat him. If you really want to deal with him, we can't use our own people."],["","Cross's furrowed brow relaxed."],["Cross","Although this is a last resort, in such a desperate situation, there's no time to worry about that. Sand Whale... and that Victor Ruark, who's probably laughing at me right now... You'll soon regret everything you've done."],["","Ridgewald was taken aback. This was not the purpose of her trip. If Sand Whale gets involved, they won't be able to find the \"treasure.\""],["Ridgewald","No, boss, maybe you should consider that Sand Whale..."],["","The electronic door's hum suddenly interrupted their conversation. Victoria stood expressionless at the doorway, coldly watching Ridgewald, who still sat with a confident swagger."],["Cross","Lieutenant? You're just in time. Regarding the suggestion you made earlier, I think we still have room for discussion, as long as you bring Sand Whale..."],["Victoria","I'm glad you finally understand, Cross, but first let me complete another important task."],["Cross","What?"],["","Victoria made a gesture, and several DLAF soldiers suddenly rushed in, pinning Ridgewald to the ground before she could react."],["Ridgewald","What's the meaning of this?! What are you trying to do?!"],["Victoria","Long time no see, SA13014. I didn't expect you to deliver yourself to me so willingly—"],["","The communicator interface is displaying a successfully sent email. The signature is blank, and the sending address is the Skynet address of the Border Police Bureau."],["","The email contains only three short lines, yet the content easily shatters Ridgewald's pretense at the police station."],["","Sand Whale leisurely reclined on the sofa, savoring his masterpiece, with the scene of Ridgewald's arrest already playing out in his mind, causing a slight smile to form at the corner of his mouth. It wasn't until he heard footsteps nearby that he discreetly turned off the screen."],["Egbert","Strange, Ridge should have been out by now. Why hasn't she contacted me?"],["Sand Whale","Is your friend the type to report everything? That's quite surprising."],["Egbert","Not really, but this operation is special... I should contact her."],["Sand Whale","If she's dealing with some unforeseen circumstances, your communication request might be untimely."],["Egbert","...Damn, we should have gone with her!"],["","Sand Whale chuckled softly, sitting up from the sofa and straightening his collar."],["Sand Whale","Don't overthink it. Her disguise is flawless, nothing will happen. Instead, have you prepared to welcome our \"Commander\"?"],["Egbert","What do I need to prepare for? You'll be the one negotiating with him later. I just need to make sure you don't conspire with that guy against us."],["Sand Whale","...You have a really clear understanding of your role."],["","Knock, knock, knock—someone was at the door to the private room. Sand Whale and Egbert exchanged a glance and straightened their backs. The door slowly opened, and His Excellency the \"Commander\" entered with a subordinate."],["","Sand Whale stood up to greet him, while the \"Commander\" merely nodded slightly in greeting after sitting down opposite him."],["","However, to everyone's surprise, after the \"Commander\" sat down, he took out a cigarette case from his pocket and slid it across the table to Sand Whale."],["Ruark","\"Silco,\" the satin cigarette that's all the rage locally. Coveted in political and business circles, it's priceless. Really hard to get your hands on. Care to try?"],["Sand Whale","I'm flattered, Commander."],["","Sand Whale smiled as he picked up the silver-engraved cigarette case and lit one for himself. Soon, the room was filled with smoke as smooth as silk."],["","He showed a look of surprise, then slid his lighter back. Ruark understood and lit one for himself as well."],["Sand Whale","Ah... truly smooth."],["Ruark","This meeting was arranged in a rush, so I didn't have time to prepare a proper gift—I'm glad you like it."],["Sand Whale","Apologies, sir, our time is limited. The matters we wish to discuss with you are as numerous as the stars, so we had to meet with you as soon as possible."],["Ruark","No problem. I'm also quite interested in the renowned \"Sand Whale.\" But I was a bit surprised when Frank said you wanted to see me..."],["Sand Whale","Haha, I just think that something as elusive as \"treasure\" can only fully reveal its value in front of someone who truly understands it."],["","The two chatted casually, both tacitly avoiding mentioning the name that should have been discussed."],["Ruark","\"Treasure\"... It seems this is the theme of our meeting?"],["Sand Whale","To be honest, I've spent a lot of resources searching for its whereabouts, but to no avail, so I had to come to you for help."],["Ruark","Me? What does this have to do with me?"],["Sand Whale","Of course, the \"treasure\" is ultimately a product of DL technology. Within the DL, its code name is \"Legacy.\" Have you heard of it?"],["Ruark","The Legacy..."],["","Sand Whale noticed the slightly puzzled expression on Ruark's face and couldn't help but feel a tinge of disappointment. It seems that even high-ranking officers in the border defense forces may not have access to the military's secrets."],["Ruark","I don't have much experience in the tech field, but if you're interested in this \"Legacy,\" I can make some inquiries."],["Sand Whale","Sir, you truly are a born leader..."],["Ruark","But in exchange..."],["Sand Whale","From now on, we'll be bound by an unbreakable bond..."],["","Ruark shook his head with a smile, took a deep drag of his cigarette, blowing out a smoke ring."],["Ruark","I know what you did to Cross, Sand Whale, but no matter. When someone sits in a high position for too long, they tend to forget who they really are. He needs some time in prison to reflect."],["Ruark","Unlike Cross, you possess the strategy and courage he lacks, yet you haven't forgotten the boundaries of your power. I think... together we can create a future that satisfies us both."],["Sand Whale","Thank you for your trust, Commander."],["","The two had a pleasant conversation, and Sand Whale even instructed Egbert to open a bottle of the good stuff to liven things up. After three rounds of drinks, Ruark finally stood up to take his leave."],["","Out of Sand Whale's sight, the polite smile that Ruark always wore quickly faded."],["Ruark's Adjutant","Commander, we just received the scouting report. Sand Whale indeed only brought one person. This is a great opportunity to catch him."],["Ruark","Don't rush. The timing isn't right. We need to find a legitimate reason to send him in, so it won't hinder us from using his reputation to take over the assets left by Cross."],["Ruark","By the way, have you found anything new about his background?"],["Ruark's Adjutant","Uh... Sorry, Commander, very few people know about Sand Whale's origins. We are still investigating."],["Ruark","Speed up the process. Only by working out the opponent's weaknesses can we effectively strike."],["Ruark's Adjutant","Yes."]],"468281101":[["","Border Base Commander's Office"],["Ruark","I can hardly remember how many times you've taken action without my permission, Lieutenant Victoria. Is challenging disciplinary authority your life's creed?"],["Ruark","Issuing a warrant for an ordinary person with no criminal record... Ha, did this poor Sand Whale inadvertently offend your dignity, Lieutenant?"],["Victoria","......"],["Victoria","We have no personal grievances, but Sand Whale is suspected of stealing DL's technological secrets and must be captured for investigation. I have already handed his case over to the relevant department. Sir, you no longer have the authority to inquire."],["","Ruark's nerves were triggered by the words \"technological secrets,\" and he reflectively blurted out a single word."],["Ruark","The Legacy..."],["","Victoria heard it. She was a bit puzzled but quickly hid her expression."],["Victoria","Sir, this is highly confidential. Please do not mention it lightly, or everyone will know... Hmph, there's no guarantee you won't be held accountable by the relevant departments."],["","Ruark stood up, paced over to Victoria, and after a long silence, slowly began to speak."],["Ruark","I know you've always been resentful about being transferred to the border defense forces, Victoria. You've been desperately trying to prove your abilities, hoping to achieve merits and return to your original unit as soon as possible."],["Ruark","But have you not considered? As your direct superior, my evaluation of you can greatly influence the determination of your merits."],["Ruark","I don't intend to keep you here against your will, provided you stop recklessly violating my rules."],["Ruark","If you understand what I mean, then organize everything you've found so far—Sand Whale, the Legacy, don't leave anything out. Report to me, then await the Commander's orders."],["","Victoria kept her gaze fixed on the neatly arranged badges on Ruark's desk, silently waiting for his lengthy speech to end. As soon as he finished, she let out a cold laugh."],["Victoria","This concerns confidential DL intelligence, and I cannot disclose anything, sir. I have no objections to any punishment you may impose, but there's one thing I want to remind you of—"],["Victoria","The discipline of the DLAF binds every soldier within it. It is our unshakable mountain, our irreversible justice."],["Victoria","You'd better pray you never cross the minefield it marks, or the punishment it brings down will be far more severe than any threat you could make, Commander."],["Ruark","Victoria, you...!"],["Victoria","I have other tasks, Commander. Excuse me."],["","With a loud bang, Victoria slammed the door and left. Ruark gritted his teeth, his tightly clenched fists crackling."],["","Anger urged him to fly into a rage, but thinking of the plan that had just taken shape in his mind, he forced himself to calm down and summoned the adjutant."],["Ruark's Adjutant","...That's roughly the situation. The officer apologizes for the warrant. Lieutenant Victoria always charges ahead recklessly. It's been a constant headache for the Commander."],["Sand Whale","No problem, I have great trust in the Commander... and a bit of admiration, heh. To tolerate a little lieutenant's lawlessness despite his status shows real magnanimity."],["Ruark's Adjutant","Lieutenant Victoria holds a kind of special status here. After all, before her transfer she served that Governor, the kind of person everyone must show some respect..."],["Ruark's Adjutant","Therefore, the Commander's suggestion is that if you play along, you might be able to obtain more information about the \"treasure\" from the Lieutenant."],["Sand Whale","...Heh, I understand. Then please thank the officer for me. This intelligence has been a great help."],["","Sand Whale's smile ceased the moment the communication was cut off. Thoughts rapidly began to surge in his mind."],["","This is indeed a perfect opportunity for him to continue the conversation with Victoria that was interrupted last time. But he also understands that Ruark is not a trustworthy partner."],["","Just how many plots lay buried beneath all this intrigue—he could not even guess."],["","But does he have any other choice? Having come this far, he's very close to the final answer... Can he really give up this shortcut and seek another path?"],["","The iron door of the depot was suddenly pulled open a crack, and Egbert returned from the night, bringing back food. Ever since the warrant for Sand Whale was issued, they had been living life on the run."],["Sand Whale","You're back? Why so late today? I'm sure if you were a minute later, you might have only found my corpse. Or rather, a bunch of skin and bones..."],["","Sand Whale rummaged through the food with both hands, not noticing Egbert standing in front of him slowly drawing a gun, until he heard a sudden click."],["Sand Whale","...Tsk, my miserable fate is as consistent as ever."],["Egbert","My patience is spent, Sand Whale."],["Sand Whale","Stay calm, Egbert... Yes, the fact that Ridgewald hasn't joined us likely means something happened to her. What we should do now is figure out a rescue plan, not turn on each other..."],["Egbert","I've already contacted Eller and Meritus. They'll be here soon, and then we'll go rescue her together."],["Sand Whale","......"],["Sand Whale","Ridge's accident has nothing to do with me. You have to believe me."],["Egbert","She agreed to cooperate under your persuasion and disguised herself to get into prison under your instructions—then something went wrong."],["Sand Whale","I'm also currently wanted. You've witnessed how relentless the police have been in pursuing us these past few days. Isn't that enough to prove my innocence?"],["Egbert","If this is your ruse, it makes perfect sense—Sand Whale, I've had enough of your lies."],["Egbert","The thing I regret most now is not shooting you when she agreed to your plan... To me, she's the most important... and I just watched her jump into the trap you set!"],["","Sand Whale's pupils contracted suddenly as he saw Egbert's finger on the trigger begin to curl."],["Sand Whale","Think, Egbert. You need me. Breaking through those heavy DLAF defenses to infiltrate the prison—it isn't simple. You lack firepower; what you need is a strategy."],["Egbert","Your strategy may send us to hell—!"],["","Egbert almost shouted this sentence, excitedly pressing the muzzle against Sand Whale's temple, forcefully squeezing the depression, causing Sand Whale's voice to start changing tone."],["Sand Whale","I can take you to find Ridgewald right now! Now! Immediately! At once!!"],["Egbert","Liar! You're trying to trick me again! You're always wearing a mask to deceive everyone! I was a fool to trust you—!"],["","*bang*"],["","Egbert lay on the ground, his heavy breathing and pounding heart consuming almost all of his ability to think. He looked at Sand Whale looming over him, momentarily unable to react. What just happened?"],["","It wasn't until blood slowly dripped down the side of Sand Whale's face onto him that he snapped back to reality and his strength returned."],["","What did you do..."],["DL Police","Listen up, people inside! Consider that shot a warning. You are surrounded! Do not resist—put down your weapons and come out quietly. The next round won't be just a single bullet!"],["Egbert","Wh-What's happening?!"],["","Egbert was dumbfounded. Sand Whale... just helped him dodge a bullet?! Soon, Egbert heard the familiar sound of sirens blaring. The red and blue lights burst in from the windows of the old depot, spinning wildly on the surrounding walls."],["Sand Whale","Ah... I knew I'd have to take this hit. Too bad it wasn't my face. My back of the head is much more important than my face..."],["Egbert","What's going on?! Sand Whale! How did they find this place?! Was it you—"],["Sand Whale","Ha! I told you—now I'll take you to find Ridgewald."],["","Sand Whale clutched the back of its head and crawled into the pile of food to retrieve his communicator. Unfortunately, the poor device had its screen shattered by the excited Egbert, but it was somehow still functional."],["","A few scattered words and phrases could still be seen on the screen. Egbert carefully discerned them: \"Sand Whale,\" \"depot,\" \"fish,\" \"already\"..."],["Sand Whale","The fish has already beached—let's go, Egbert, it's time for us to go ashore."],["","Police Station Interrogation Room"],["Victoria","You... you... how could it possibly be you!? You're the Sand Whale?!"],["Sand Whale","Hi... It's been a while, Lieutenant. Seeing you still so energetic is truly disheartening."],["","Sand Whale responded, somewhat enfeebled. A few rough bandages were wrapped around his head, with a patch of fresh blood seeping from the wound at the back of his head, soaking the cloth."],["","His two hands and feet are bound to the chair, unable to move, yet it doesn't stop him from chatting away."],["Victoria","Will Sander! Is this your scheme?"],["Sand Whale","This is the righteous hammer of the wise and mighty officer, and also the consequence of my own lax discipline... Ah, don't let me catch the bastard who anonymously leaked my whereabouts."],["Victoria","Stop playing word games with me!"],["","Victoria slammed the table hard, supporting her upper body with a piercing gaze."],["Victoria","\"Treasure,\" \"Legacy,\" \"Sand Whale\"... What exactly is your purpose? And how do you know of such confidential information? Who sent you?"],["Sand Whale","That's quite a lot of questions, Lieutenant. How about we prioritize them first... Tsh—!"],["","Victoria grabbed the bandage on Sand Whale's head with one hand, her fingers pressing right on the bullet-grazed wound, causing the bloodstain to slowly spread. Sand Whale jolted violently, but unable to move due to the restraints, soon broke out in a cold sweat."],["Victoria","Answer me properly, no nonsense. Who sent you?"],["Sand Whale","Huff—huff—huff—"],["","Sand Whale found it difficult to speak and could only breathe deeply to cope with the pain. Victoria sneered and released her grip. Sand Whale lowered his head, his mind momentarily desensitized."],["","In the next second, Victoria's fist landed on his stomach, instantly triggering a spasm."],["Victoria","...How pitiful, Will Sander. Do you still remember what I said to you back then?"],["Victoria","\"If you don't give me the answer I want in five seconds, this blade will end you.\" Unfortunately, you've already exhausted my trust. This time, you'll receive no mercy. Lie again, and your life will be ended, slowly."],["Sand Whale","Ugh—!"],["","Sand Whale's eyes widened, a metallic taste rising in his throat as the numbness in his brain gradually spread throughout his body. Suddenly, the alarm outside the interrogation room blared loudly, signaling an emergency assembly."],["Victoria's Adjutant","Lieutenant, there has been intense conflict in the eastern region of the Foren River. We've received a distress signal from the local defense force outpost. Do you need to assist the police in providing support?"],["Victoria","Let them coordinate their own rescue teams. Today, I'm here only for the \"Sand Whale.\""],["Victoria's Adjutant","...Yes."],["","Victoria grabbed Sand Whale's hair, forcing him to look up, only to see his eyes half-closed and unable to focus."],["Victoria","You can't escape anymore. I have plenty of time to deal with you. But as long as you tell me who sent you..."],["Sand Whale","Lukmund..."],["Victoria","I can—What?! What did you just say?"],["Sand Whale","Lord Lukmund... I am carrying out a secret mission he assigned... Victoria, from now on, you must ensure that our conversation is not overheard by anyone, and you must forget everything after you hear it."],["","Victoria, shocked, let go and stumbled back."],["Victoria","No... Impossible! How could you be sent by him?! I need to confirm with my superiors..."],["Sand Whale","Don't make any rash moves. There's a mole within the DL, but he doesn't know his identity has been suspected. If you leak my identity and mission, it will surely alert him."],["Victoria","What exactly are you trying to do...?"],["Sand Whale","Listen carefully, the Legacy was taken by a UNCS Agent assisted by the mole during that great battle, but the DL's higher-ups are unaware of this. I must retrieve the Legacy before the situation escalates, or you will inevitably be implicated."],["Victoria","Impossible! No one can break through her defenses... who could possibly seize the Legacy? What UNCS agent can defeat the DL's \"Super Pilot\"?!"],["Sand Whale","......"],["","Sand Whale was silent. He silently gazed at Victoria, his dark eyes rippling with something that left Victoria quite puzzled. After a moment, he threw back his head and laughed heartily."],["Victoria","What? What's so funny?"],["Sand Whale","Haha... Hahaha... No... No, no, I just find it... ironic, you're kept in the dark just like them..."],["Victoria","...You're lying, I never received any message to cooperate with your actions, you can't be someone sent by Lukmund—"],["Sand Whale","...Do you really think being transferred to the border was a random decision?"],["Victoria","...What do you mean?! What do you know?!"],["Sand Whale","Heh... Hehe... Victoria, the higher-ups have long been aware of the dealings between Ruark and Cross. You may not have received any information about cooperating with my actions, but I have received orders to assist you in exposing Ruark's crimes!"],["Victoria","W-What?! Are you saying that my demotion and transfer to the border guard was also part of the higher-ups' plan?"],["Victoria","Impossible! If this was a task given to me by the higher-ups, there's no way they wouldn't reveal even a hint of it to me—"],["Sand Whale","Hmm... Then you should ask yourself what you might have done before to disappoint the people above."],["Victoria","......"],["","Victoria fell silent, utterly confused. Sand Whale's words were logical and irrefutable, but her deeply rooted intuition told her not to let her guard down."],["Sand Whale","In the right pocket of my coat, there's a gift prepared for you—it was taken out during the search and is now kept in the evidence room."],["Victoria","...What gift? Will Sander, what trick are you trying to pull?"],["Sand Whale","Heh, it's the evidence you've been eagerly waiting for."],["Sand Whale","Go take a look, you'll thank me. I'm stuck here and can't escape anyway, what are you afraid of?"],["Victoria","......"],["Sand Whale","Turn off the light for me before you leave. I need... a few minutes of rest."],["","Victoria hesitated for a moment, but ultimately decided to quickly go and check."],["","Darkness envelopes everything... The Sand Whale hears nothing but the sound of his own labored breathing. Blood mixes with sweat as it trickles down his face, stinging his wounds before gathering on his chin and dropping to the floor below in a continuous, steady drip."],["","Tap—tap—tap. Sudden footsteps..."],["","...Returning to the present, Ruark is silently listening to Sand Whale's story."],["","Spreading rumors of a treasure—the so-called Legacy—and baiting mercs to search for it, assuming the alias \"Will Sander,\" setting his sights on the DL, attempting to team up with Commander Ruark..."],["","All the way up to the moment he was imprisoned."],["","Sand Whale's narrative was very detailed, sometimes even going as far to explain his inner thoughts and feelings. After he finished, neither of them spoke again for a not-too-long, not-too-short two minutes."],["","It wasn't until he burst into a fit of strong coughing from overusing his voice that the increasingly enfeebled man chose to break the silence again."],["Sand Whale","If this story is somewhat unexpected for you, could you pour me a glass of water as encouragement from the audience?"],["Ruark","Heh, a secret agent... daring to brave the storm of the Legacy affair?"],["","Sand Whale didn't respond, just tilted his head and smiled, seeming to see the humor as well."],["Ruark","You are a master of manipulating intelligence, Sand Whale. The information, whether true or false, always seems somewhat credible after your arrangement. But I'm not that foolish. I won't be deceived by the stories you've carefully prepared, nor will I waste time verifying whether what you say is true or false."],["Ruark","The border turmoil has been going on for some time. It's time to end it, with your capture as the final chapter, don't you think?"],["Sand Whale","...Sir."],["Sand Whale","By the way, do you know the origin of the name \"Sand Whale\"?"],["Ruark","Of course. Information is like a sea of sand, and you feed on it, always consuming both the abundant and the precious... Quite an interesting naming method. Is this your own creation?"],["Sand Whale","Yes, sir. It seems you have a good eye for appreciation. A whale is a massive creature, and if it could swim in a sea of sand... The sand flows slowly, and those standing on it will only realize it was there long after it has left."],["Sand Whale","Whether it wants to spend a pleasant time with you or hunt you down... you'll only know the moment the sand sinks."],["","Ruark shrugged. He might have sensed the metaphor in Sand Whale's words, but the obvious victory at hand made him reluctant to ponder deeply."],["Ruark","...A very... imaginative description, Mr. Sand Whale, but now it's time for us to change venues. You'll like it there, I promise—"],["Ruark","Bring two people to escort the prisoner back to base."],["","Ruark gave instructions into the communicator on his collar."],["Sand Whale","From now on, the \"Sand Whale\" mantle is yours, sir... Don't ruin my reputation."],["Ruark","Heh, don't be discouraged, Sand Whale. We still have many issues to reach a consensus on, and you still have room to negotiate..."],["","The sudden hum of the electronic door opening interrupted Ruark, who turned around to see an unexpected person—Victoria, marching into the interrogation room with a large group of DLAF soldiers behind her."],["Ruark","What is the meaning of this, Lieutenant Victoria?"],["","Victoria coldly took out a voice recorder, turned the external speaker volume to maximum, and pressed the play button."],["","\"Treasure... It seems this is the theme of our meeting?\"... \"I don't have much experience in the tech field, but if you're interested in this 'Legacy,' I can make some inquiries\"..."],["","Ruark was instantly incredulous, staring in shock at Sand Whale, who gave him a friendly smile and exaggeratedly mouthed the word \"surprise.\""],["","The recorder was still playing, capturing every word of the conversation between Ruark and Sand Whale that day, each word turning into a sharp sword in Victoria's hand."],["Victoria","...Victor Ruark, you are hereby charged with multiple offenses, including corruption, abuse of power, and unauthorized disclosure of military secrets. I am placing you under arrest to be delivered to the Military Council for judgment."],["Ruark","Victoria, I am your superior! You have no right to—"],["Victoria","Take him away."],["Ruark","Victoria! You can't do this to me! I am innocent! I am your superior! I am the commander of this base! I order you—!"],["","Ruark's voice slowly faded away outside the door. Victoria watched with an aloof expression as he was taken away in a most undignified manner, listening to his curses without a single response."],["Sand Whale","You won... Lieutenant. With my testimony, if you can convince Cross to attend the hearing, Ruark's guilt will be undeniable."],["Victoria","And you think you can earn my trust by assisting in the prosecution?"],["Sand Whale","...I thought you would be very pleased with the gift I prepared for you."],["Victoria","Heh, Will Sander... or perhaps you really are the Sand Whale. This recorder cannot completely clear you of suspicion. As for your situation, I will conduct a more detailed investigation."],["Victoria","You better not be deceiving me, or this time I definitely won't let you leave here alive."],["Victoria's Adjutant","Lieutenant! This is bad! The radar shows a group of unknown ST signals approaching! Most of the police force has been dispatched to support the eastern Foren River—we need your command!"],["Victoria","What?! How could this happen now—"],["Sand Whale","It seems to be a feint, Lieutenant. Their real target is here, and if we don't respond properly... many people could die."],["Victoria","...I'll be there as soon as I can."],["","Victoria quickly leaves the interrogation room, giving orders as she walks."],["Victoria","Escort the guy from the interrogation room back to the cell. A1 Squad, gather your members and prepare to move out immediately!"],["","As Victoria's voice gradually faded into the distance, Sand Whale lowered his head, laughter slowly bubbling up from his throat."],["","He spat out a thin blade, cutting the restraints on his wrist, then swung his numb arm to get the blood circulating."],["Sand Whale","Hey, Meritus... or is it Eller? Come on, let's have some fun together."]],"468281301":[["Mercenary","Boss Eller! It's bad—we must retreat! Otherwise, our brothers are done for!"],["Eller","No way! We've already paid such a high price, we must rescue Ridgewald and the others no matter what!"],["","The DLAF pressed its advantage, their firepower growing ever more intense. Eller's unit was blasted apart, shattered and routed. With Kong's magazine nearly empty, Eller and her subordinates could only take cover behind ruined barricades, waiting for a chance to launch another desperate assault."],["Mercenary","But boss! If we escape, we'll still have another chance. If you get caught, they really have no hope!"],["Eller","......"],["","Eller gritted her teeth in silence. Such a decision was still too heavy for her."],["","The situation on the island changes rapidly. If she chooses to leave this time and doesn't hold on, when will she have another chance to save her younger siblings?"],["","If she fights harder and acts more recklessly, could she perhaps gain a slim chance for Ridge and Egbert to return safely to her side?"],["Eller","...You all go."],["Mercenary","B-Boss?!"],["Eller","You, take them and go, meet up with Meritus, I'll cover the rear."],["Mercenary","Are you crazy, Boss? If we leave, we leave together, otherwise the DLAF will definitely capture you—"],["Eller","You're right. If we all fall here, it's over, but I can't leave the two of them behind."],["Eller","Listen carefully, after retreating, go meet up with Meritus. He knows what to do—go!"],["Mercenary","No! Boss, I can't leave you behind—!"],["Eller","Go! This is an order."],["Mercenary","Boss!"],["","Boom! A smoke grenade descends from the sky, interrupting the two arguing comrades. Eller instantly bursts into action, her finger already on the trigger."],["???","...Sister Eller? Sister Eller! Is that you?"],["Eller","Egbert?! Is that you?! Have you been rescued?! Where are you?!"],["Egbert","No time to explain, quickly follow the route I sent you to get out of here. We'll meet at area N10, hurry!"],["Eller","Alright, stay safe—we're retreating immediately!"],["","Meanwhile, on the other side of the battlefield."],["DL Soldier","Lieutenant! They're retreating!"],["Victoria","Catch up to them, and make sure to capture them alive—I have questions to ask."],["DL Soldier","Understood!"],["","Victoria pulled the control lever to accelerate with full force; the smoke on the battlefield was sliced in half by her ST."],["","Her attention was fully drawn to the target ahead, when suddenly the entire cockpit shook violently—someone had sniped her ST. She quickly found cover and prepared to retaliate."],["DL Soldier","Lieutenant? Are you okay?!"],["Victoria","I'm fine, there are still some stragglers. I'll handle them, you guys go after the others!"],["DL Soldier","Lieutenant, someone is covering their escape, and we've lost their coordinates!"],["Victoria","Damn it—! Who on earth...?!"],["Victoria","Could it be...? No... this is bad, go back! All team members! Return to the police station! Quickly! Full speed back to the station—!"],["","Sand Whale leaped down from the cockpit, the exertion pulling agonizingly at his multiple wounds. The moment he landed, he staggered, unable to conceal the pain."],["","Click. A familiar sound yanked him back to his senses. He instantly forgot the pain, and turning back with a dumbfounded look, he saw Egbert, standing in the shadow of the ST. He held a gun—pointing straight at the Sand Whale's heart."],["Sand Whale","...You must remember, Egbert. It was when I came out that I conveniently opened the cell door for you. That's the only reason you're able to be standing here right now, pointing a gun at me."],["Sand Whale","Imagine if you were executed for doing a good deed, would you die with regrets?"],["Egbert","I remember clearly, it was when you passed by my cell door that I grabbed you and threatened you with a knife to make you open the door for me."],["","Sand Whale shrugged after his lie was exposed—this action tugged at his battered body, causing him to grimace in pain."],["Sand Whale","Tsh... But still, without my help, you wouldn't be enjoying freedom right now..."],["","Egbert pursed his lips, flipped his wrist, and handed the gunstock to Sand Whale. Sand Whale widened his eyes slightly, somewhat puzzled."],["Egbert","I once shot you, if you can't let it go, you can shoot me too."],["Sand Whale","...Ah."],["Sand Whale","An eye-for-an-eye kind of revenge is no longer the way, my friend. Besides, that shot to the back of my head wasn't your doing, so I bear no grudge."],["Egbert","...I've struck you, threatened you, again and again. You can hold me accountable any way you see fit."],["Sand Whale","Not at all, there's no longer anything between us; we can now go our separate ways."],["","Sand Whale had no intention of taking the gun. He turned around to leave."],["Egbert","...Sand Whale! Ridgewald's still locked up in the slammer!"],["","Sand Whale's distant silhouette came to a halt."],["Egbert","You promised to take me to see her."],["","Egbert's expression was stubborn, but the hand resting in mid-air trembled slightly."],["","Was this the right thing to do? Was it right to bury his rage towards Sand Whale and request his help regardless?"],["","Sand Whale is a cunning man, but also a powerful one. He manipulates everyone, controlling all the pieces to advance toward the outcome he desires. Right now, he is exactly the ally Egbert needs."],["","Faced with those formidable DLAF forces, Egbert truly has no other choice... But will the one who holds all the cards really listen to the one who holds none?"],["Egbert","I no longer wish to pursue the truth about Ridge's capture. Sand Whale, regardless of the role you played in that matter, I'll leave it be. I just want to rescue her."],["Sand Whale","......"],["Egbert","Do you have any other motives? This time, I willingly become your pawn, use me wherever you see fit... as long as you're willing to help rescue her."],["Sand Whale","Ah... I'm somewhat aware of Miss Ridgewald's situation. She doesn't deserve to die, and she'll surely be released after serving her sentence."],["Egbert","Ridgewald is not someone who'll sit idly by. She will find a way to escape, and the DLAF will have countless reasons to execute her on the spot. I can't wait until then."],["Sand Whale","...Hmm."],["???","If you can really help rescue Ridge, then we'll owe you big time, Sand Whale—all of us."],["Egbert","...! Eller..."],["","Eller steps out from the shadows, her entire right arm wrapped in bandages."],["Eller","I've heard of your skills, and you've proven your abilities to me. I'm willing to place my trust in you—as long as you help this time, we can do something for you in the future. As long as it doesn't harm us both, anything goes."],["Eller","I'm their leader, and my word is my bond."],["","Sand Whale slowly turned around, his gaze silently moving back and forth between Eller and Egbert, then turned again to look at the distant sunset."],["","After a moment, he smacked his palm with his fist. He turned around, smiling."],["Sand Whale","If this is the hand of destiny at work, it wouldn't hurt to go along with it for once."],["Egbert","Y-you agree!?"],["Sand Whale","Hey, I left something for that lieutenant. I originally just wanted to get my own back for how harshly she treated me, but who would've thought... Without that thing, it would probably take a long time to wait for a good chance to rescue Miss Ridgewald."]],"468285101":[["","Police Station Interrogation Room"],["","Victoria suppressed her fury as she faced the wall of the interrogation room. This was her third time in front of this wall since her return, and there was now an extra line scrawled in blood."],["","The elegant script showed no hesitation; the person who wrote this line must have mulled over the phrase countless times in their mind—\"Fish Returns to the Sand-Sea,\" that's the translation of the line."],["Victoria's Adjutant","Lieutenant, the person has been brought in."],["","A rustling sound came from behind as the soldier was restraining the prisoner to the chair."],["Ridgewald","Wow—is that blood? Whose handiwork is it?"],["Victoria","You know him—Will Sander, or as you prefer to call him, \"Sand Whale.\""],["","Victoria turned around and sat across from the new prisoner. As she finished speaking, she noticed Ridgewald's eyes light up."],["Ridgewald","Did you capture him too? Can I see him? Let me see him—I promise to cooperate with your questioning!"],["Victoria","I'm sorry."],["Victoria","He was briefly interrogated in this room... sitting right where you are now."],["Ridgewald","......"],["","Ridgewald paused, glanced at the bloody words behind Victoria, and then burst into laughter."],["Ridgewald","Hahaha, you got played by him too! Interesting, interesting... Sand Whale... you really are an incredible guy..."],["","Though there was a hint of amusement in her tone, Ridgewald's face showed little sign of delight."],["Victoria","Let's get straight to the point—you're one of Sand Whale's pawns. We received an anonymous tip-off when you infiltrated, and after analysis, the Skynet address of the sender matched the Skynet address used when he anonymously reported himself this time."],["Ridgewald","I know. I know who's plotting against me."],["Victoria","So, don't you want revenge?"],["Ridgewald","...Working with guys like you is risky. I have the information you want, which is why I can still sit here and talk to you. But once I lose my value to you, I'm afraid I'll be thrown into prison and forgotten, right?"],["Victoria","If you cooperate, I can try to make a case for you. Bring us Sand Whale and redeem yourself. Freedom will come sooner than you think."],["","Ridgewald remains silent, seemingly contemplating the credibility of Victoria's words."],["Ridgewald","...Alright, although I don't trust you that much, you're lucky—my dislike for Sand Whale far exceeds my dislike for you right now. So, what do you want to know?"],["Victoria","Everything—all that happened between you and Sand Whale."],["Ridgewald","It's a long story... Ah, not that long. After all, I've only known that bastard for a few days."],["Ridgewald","You know I was originally employed by Cross. After Cross had an incident, Sand Whale plotted to seize his assets, even persuading Cross's most loyal subordinates... Ha, but that's just a facade, a cover for his true intentions."],["","Yes... Victoria closed her eyes. His true intention is..."],["Ridgewald","\"Treasure.\" He came in search of the \"treasure.\""],["Victoria","......"],["Ridgewald","He inquired about the \"treasure\" from various sources, and after consolidating all the information, he determined that he should start with the DL. He wanted to find a big shot in the DLAF and ask them to gather information..."],["Victoria","Stop, we can leave that part aside for now. I've already confirmed his intentions."],["Victoria","Do you know anything else about him personally?"],["Ridgewald","Him personally? Just rumors. You want me to sit here and share gossip? I didn't take you for the type."],["Victoria","Isn't there anything else? We can't catch him with just this..."],["Ridgewald","Use \"treasure\" to lure him. If there's anything that'll grab his attention, it's that."],["","Victoria started to get a headache, unwilling to explain to Ridgewald how Sand Whale risked his life and finally succeeded in uncovering the whereabouts of the Legacy."],["","By now the situation had spiraled beyond her control. She alone could not turn the tide. Through her reluctance, her soldier's principles urged her forward. She stepped out to make the call."],["Victoria","The whereabouts of the Legacy have been leaked, Ma'at. I request that this matter be handled seriously."],["Ma'at","......"],["Victoria","If you're interested in the details, you can attend the hearing later to listen to my testimony. Our immediate priority is to find a way to prevent any impending incidents. Sand Whale might make a move..."],["Ma'at","No one can defeat Aida Diaz, so you don't need to worry. Immediately transfer all evidence and witnesses related to this matter to Thepia, and submit an additional report. I will head over to take over the follow-up work."],["","That's it. Ma'at has always been someone to remain calm in a crisis."],["","Victoria took a deep breath. She wanted to say something more, or fight for something, but no matter how eloquently she spoke, it was all in vain given the current situation."],["","Unless she immediately captures Sand Whale."],["Victoria","Got it."],["","On the helipad, the fierce wind from the landing helicopter continuously sliced across Victoria's face. Behind her, Ridgewald impatiently tried to brush away her hair as it flapped in her face, but she remained steadfast."],["","The propeller slowly came to a stop. Victoria made a gesture. The soldiers understood and escorted Ridgewald forward for the handover."],["DL Soldier","Thank you for your support, Lieutenant. We will depart immediately."],["Victoria","Don't let your guard down on the way; she is not an ordinary prisoner."],["DL Soldier","Understood. We have prepared a strong anesthetic. When she wakes up, she'll find herself in a place she can't escape from."],["Victoria","Go ahead, and have a safe journey."],["","The propeller slowly started to turn again, spinning faster and faster, lifting the massive cabin into the distance. Victoria watched the fleet in silence until they became a cluster of tiny dots in the sky."],["Victoria","Take Ruark to the interrogation room. Bring forward the scheduled questioning. It's time we had a good talk."],["","Inside the helicopter cabin, there was silence. The pilot skillfully operated the lever, occasionally confirming the route with a companion, while Ridgewald lay unconscious in the back seat."],["","After a while, perhaps out of boredom, the soldier in the co-pilot seat started humming a song. The pilot couldn't help but laugh upon hearing it, and just as he was about to say something, the singing stopped."],["Pilot","Haha, what? I didn't even say anything this time! Could it be that you're becoming aware of your tone-deaf singing...?"],["","The pilot turned his head with a smile, only to see a metallic glint rushing toward his face. He leapt backward instinctively."],["Pilot","What's happening?!"],["","As he shouted in confusion, he saw Ridgewald, her hands slick with blood. She shifted her stance, gripped the blade again, and drove it toward him. The prisoner hadn't been sedated at all; she'd used pain to resist its effects."],["Pilot","Don't kill me! Please! I'll do whatever you say! Just don't kill me, don't kill me! Ahhh! Ahhhhh—!"],["","Ridgewald was so annoyed by his shouting that it gave him a headache. She struck the pilot unconscious with a chop and kicked him aside."],["Ridgewald","Ugh, pack it in! You're a grown man—act like one!"],["","The moment the pilot went down, the chopper began losing altitude in a race against time."],["","Ridgewald trembled as she sat in the pilot's seat, gripping the control stick tightly. The cut on her palm sent a piercing pain, but it wasn't enough to stop her. She shook her head vigorously, trying to stay alert."],["","Come on, let it blaze through you, Ridgewald. This escape... This intensity... Hold onto this feeling, the feeling of being alive!"],["DL Soldier","A7 Special Operations Team calling base! A7 Special Operations Team calling base! Emergency! Emergency! Ridgewald has hijacked the helicopter and deviated from the original course! Requesting support! Requesting support!"],["Victoria","What?! Wasn't she sedated? How does she still have such mobility?!"],["DL Soldier","N-no idea, sir! We've been disconnected from the main system! Requesting support—! Ah! What?! The control stick is malfunctioning?! What's going on?!"],["Victoria","Hey? Hey?! What's happening?! Answer quickly!"],["Victoria's Adjutant","Oh no, it seems that Ridgewald has taken control of the latest weapon linkage system installed on the helicopter, allowing her to hack into the operational authority of other helicopters! Lieutenant, if this continues, we'll lose the whole squad!"],["Victoria","I'll prepare to support immediately—"],["Victoria's Adjutant","Lieutenant! You must be extra careful. Most of the STs in the base are also equipped with the same linkage system, making them easily influenced by her on the battlefield!"],["Victoria","What?! What's the point of developing a system so easily manipulated by the enemy? I'll dismantle them all when I get back!"]],"468285301":[["","High-frequency red lights flashed all over the control pane. The alarm blared. Ridgewald's hands trembled uncontrollably due to excessive blood loss. She attempted a hard reset of the power system, but each time her wobbly, weak hands failed to grip the control lever."],["","In the end, she had to change her approach, struggling to prop herself up and using all her strength to slam into the control lever. This time she finally succeeded, but a more despairing reality struck—pushing the control lever to the extreme couldn't prevent the helicopter's descent."],["","Ridgewald cursed under her breath and forced herself to stay alert as she left the pilot's seat. Parachute... Parachute... There was still a glimmer of hope as long as she could find the parachute..."],["","Suddenly, her gaze was drawn to a black package hanging on the cabin wall—that had to be the parachute pack! She felt a sense of relief and immediately moved in that direction."],["","This will only lead to a quicker death."],["","Ridgewald was startled, someone was speaking!"],["Ridgewald","Who's there?!"],["","There were only three people in the helicopter. Herself, a corpse and... Suddenly, a hand grabbed her wrist."],["???","Hey, hey! Long time no see, did you miss my voice, old friend?"],["","Ridgewald's pupils suddenly contracted as she looked at the pilot she had knocked out, who was now squatting in front of her with a beaming smile, showing no sign of the previous terror."],["","The pilot waved another hand in front of her eyes in confusion."],["???","Hey hey? Have you lost so much blood that your brain can't think anymore? Don't you remember me? I am—"],["Ridgewald","Sand.... Whale!"],["Sand Whale","Huh?!"],["","Sand Whale quickly grabbed the charging Ridgewald. Her surging adrenaline made her a formidable force despite having lost so much blood—he was almost knocked over."],["","Fortunately for him, Ridgewald was nonetheless weakened, unable to exert her full, monstrous strength. After dodging her most powerful strike, Sand Whale seized the opportunity to snatch the blade from her hand and tightly lock her arms behind her."],["","With these clean and efficient grappling techniques, Sand Whale must have undergone rigorous martial arts training... And the worst part? She was only realizing it now."],["Ridgewald","Let me go! You bastard! I'm going to kill you! Traitor! Scum! I'll tear you to pieces!!"],["Sand Whale","Alright, alright, go ahead and curse—finish it now so you won't open your mouth later. Be careful not to bite your tongue in the strong wind."],["","Sand Whale's eardrums were almost pierced by the intense sound waves. He grimaced and quickly grabbed the parachute pack, strapping it onto himself. Ridgewald saw him put on the only parachute. Panic set in."],["Ridgewald","What do you mean?! Give me the parachute! You despicable scoundrel!"],["Sand Whale","With your injuries, it's best not to do high-risk actions like parachuting. Don't worry, I'll get you out safely—"],["Ridgewald","You're lying! You traitor! Do you expect me to trust you again? Dream on! Ah—!!"],["","Sand Whale suddenly pulled open the hatch, and a gust of wind rushed in instantly. Ridgewald felt as if she had been doused with an invisible bucket of water, unable to see anything, her breath taken away."],["Sand Whale","Sometimes it's best not to believe what I say..."],["","Sand Whale peeked out to visually assess the pre-designated landing spot, his hands never stopping as he securely tied Ridgewald and himself together. After a final check to ensure everything was secure, he prepared to jump."],["Sand Whale","But sometimes you just have to believe it—hahaha—!"],["Ridgewald","You...! Aaaah!!"],["","The two of them were sent flying—"],["","In that instant, Ridgewald's entire body froze—she lost all perception of the outside world. Her body trembled in extreme fear, not that she was aware."],["","Deserts, jungles, lakes, and the smoke of warfire were all laid out before her."],["","She had never felt the world so vast, nor herself so small—turns out, when one has the ability to fly, the world looks just like this."],["","The thought flashed through her mind for only a brief moment, as she quickly plummeted down, fear scattering all her thoughts. It seemed as if an invisible giant hand behind her wanted to crush her into the ground, yet a fierce wind in front of her lifted her body..."],["","She couldn't find any substantial support—except for Sand Whale behind her, but that guy was an unreliable bastard!"],["","I'm going to die... I'm going to die, going to die, going to die... This time I'm really going to die—!!"],["Ridgewald","Ahhh—!!!"],["Sand Whale","Ahhh—stop yelling! Something really might happen."],["","Sand Whale responded appropriately with a few sounds, but there was no panic in his voice. Clearly, he was a skilled parachutist, long accustomed to being surrounded by the feeling of weightlessness."],["Ridgewald","Y-y-you... what do you w-w-want to do?"],["Sand Whale","Hahaha, save some strength and hold on tight. Don't fall now."],["Sand Whale","Rest assured, I'm really here to save you. Once we land in a safe place, your friends will come to pick you up."],["Sand Whale","I don't plan on taking you as a prisoner for now. After all, I'm barely managing myself. I can't afford a burden."],["Ridgewald","A burden?! Who are you calling a burden?! You jerk, I haven't even settled the score with you yet—"],["","Ridgewald held her breath and started to struggle, swinging her hands backward as if trying to hit Sand Whale's face."],["Sand Whale","Hey! Don't move around! Our course is going to be redirected!"],["Ridgewald","Sand Whale! Go to hell... ah—!"],["Sand Whale","Don't move! We're losing balance!"],["Ridgewald","You—!"],["","Sand Whale suddenly raised his elbow and struck Ridgewald hard on the back of the head, causing her to immediately go limp."],["Sand Whale","What a pity. I should have done this sooner..."],["Sand Whale","...Although the process was quite tortuous, fortunately, the result met expectations... Should I continue to track that squad?"],["","Ridgewald groggily opened her eyes, only to see Sand Whale leaning against a tree, speaking into a communicator. What was he saying? She couldn't make heads or tails of it. She had not fully come to her senses."],["Sand Whale","...Alright, I understand. Then, I will continue tracking Ophelia's movements, rest assured."],["","Ridgewald sat up and knocked her head hard. Sand Whale quickly heard the noise she made, hung up the communication, and came over."],["Sand Whale","Hey hey? Miss Ridgewald. We're safe. Eller and the others will come to pick you up shortly."],["Sand Whale","Remember to tell Eller that our trade has officially begun."],["Ridgewald","Trade...? What... what trade did you make?"],["Sand Whale","You can ask them yourself later. I have to go. When you're weak, you have to guard against being betrayed, ha ha ha..."],["","Sand Whale shook his head with a smile and prepared to leave, ignoring Ridgewald. Ridgewald's heart skipped a beat, and she struggled to stand up."],["Ridgewald","Sand Whale! Don't get too cocky... I'll remember your face, and I'll find a chance to kill you someday, if it's the last thing I do! No one who's betrayed me has ever lived, and you... just wait..."],["","Sand Whale paused his steps and suddenly turned around. He stood under the shadow of trees, with dappled sunlight moving across his body. Ridgewald felt dizzy, her vision blurred. She struggled to make out the expression on Sand Whale's face."],["Sand Whale","Is that so? Miss Ridgewald... which face do you remember?"],["Ridgewald","I..."],["Sand Whale","Is it this one..."],["","Ridgewald's eyes widened. It was as if she were watching Sand Whale shed his own skin—yet there was no flesh beneath it. What stood before her was still a person, eerily familiar."],["Sand Whale","Or is it this one?"],["Ridgewald","...Who, who are you...really...?"],["Sand Whale","I am the \"Sand Whale\"... The \"Sand Whale,\" Miss Ridgewald."],["","The voice of the \"Sand Whale\" blurred between male and female. He took a few steps forward, shedding a layer of skin. Ridgewald instinctively stepped back—as if some unspeakable monster were drawing near."],["Sand Whale","I am the \"Sand Whale,\" and I am anyone."],["Ridgewald","No, no... you're no one... you're nobody!"],["Sand Whale","......"],["Sand Whale","Yes. You're right, my friend."],["","The \"Sand Whale\" smiled and continued on his way."],["Sand Whale","We will meet again, Miss Ridgewald. I hope when that day comes, you still remember my appearance..."],["","DL Border Base."],["","Victoria is adjusting her uniform in front of the mirror. Beside her, the adjutant is holding a stack of documents and reporting work to her."],["Victoria's Adjutant","...So, regarding the upcoming inauguration ceremony for the new base commander, do you need to familiarize yourself with the process?"],["Victoria","It's none of my concern. That's something the newcomer needs to focus on. I have more important work."],["Victoria's Adjutant","...Lieutenant, after all, this is your first meeting with the new officer. It is only reasonable to pay attention..."],["","The adjutant observed that Victoria's expression did not change, so she boldly continued speaking."],["Victoria's Adjutant","Although you reported Commander Ruark this time and contributed to the cause, you did not receive any commendation. The reason for this..."],["Victoria","Shut up."],["Victoria's Adjutant","Sorry, Lieutenant!"],["","Victoria's eyes turned cold, and she gritted her teeth silently."],["","Sand Whale... One day... one day you will fall into my hands..."],["Victoria","Let's go, the inauguration ceremony is about to begin."],["Victoria's Adjutant","Y-Yes, Lieutenant!"],["","Sand Whale sprawled on the bed, letting out a long sigh. The days of scheming and chasing had drained a lot of energy, but now that things had come to a close, he could finally rest for a while."],["","He looked at the colorful advertisements on the convenience store outside the window, and with the faint background noise filtered through the glass, he slowly closed his eyes..."],["","Twenty minutes later, he sat up out of necessity—his brain was still in a state of euphoria, and he had not the slightest hint of sleepiness."],["","He touched his face, the unmistakable dull pain seeping up from deep beneath his fingertips He jumped out of bed and walked to the dressing table."],["","First, he examined his face from different angles, showing a satisfied expression. Then he took out alcohol and tweezers from his pocket, gently lifting an inconspicuous corner behind his ear."],["Sand Whale","Hey... Now that you mention it..."],["","When Sand Whale was young, he was obsessed with this technique. At the beginning of his studies, he could change a hundred faces a day, until he received a stern reprimand from his teacher, only then would he reluctantly put his beloved masks back into the box."],["","He was addicted to playing the lives of others. No one knew what kind of pleasurable experience he gained from those pre-designed lives, but it was this pleasure that drove him to become the teacher's best student."],["","On graduation day, the teacher earnestly warned him that the longer a mask is worn, the harder it is to remove. He must never forget his original face... he must guard his heart."],["Sand Whale","Ouch, that really stings..."],["","Now, he slowly peeled off the last layer of skin from his face, revealing a slightly reddened complexion from being covered by a mask for so long."],["Anderson","Oh... hey, been a while, my friend..."],["","A strange yet familiar smile appeared on the face in the mirror, and it took him a few minutes to get used to his current appearance."],["","Then, he extended a finger."],["Anderson","The loss of four mobile squads, a drone carrier, a helicopter squad... and the border army's deployment situation..."],["Anderson","Oh, and that unlucky Ruark... The new guy in charge must be from the old defense faction, right? They'll be busy now."],["","He extended another finger."],["Anderson","Cross entrenched in the chaotic borderlands, the scandals of DL tax officials, and some insignificant underlings... Hmm, that should give the GSA a bit of leverage in its dealings with the border mercs, shouldn't it?"],["","He extended a third finger."],["Anderson","And last of all, the whereabouts of that Legacy..."],["","Anderson looked at his third extended finger, hesitated, and then withdrew it."],["Anderson","Sigh... Even after all this effort, the outcome is still not ideal..."],["Anderson","But since Miss Diaz is willing to step in, it means... the DLAF protecting the Legacy have run into some real trouble, haven't they?"],["","With this thought, Anderson shifted his gaze back to the mirror, meeting the eyes of the hollow shell of a man reflected there."],["Anderson","Truly remarkable, Miss Newman... Monitoring your whereabouts for the [Madam] is no walk in the park..."],["Anderson","However, you've always had a knack for this, haven't you?"],["","The man in the mirror gave him a gentle smile."]]};
